er holes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/18/code.py:76:   and at least one outer shell, the fused behavior does not collapse back to the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/18/code.py:173:    Build concentric diamond shells from horizontal color stripes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/18/code.py:179:    - each later stripe of height h adds a same-color diamond shell covering the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/18/code.py:183:      not erase the new shell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3e6067c3/2/code.py:37:# - 原 `label_mask(g == border)` 只适用于单一边框色；现在必须对每种非背景色分别检测矩形环组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/25/code.py:68:  nested structure and a non-zero count code, without introducing too many\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/42/code.py:30:#   1. D4/2: a border is now multicolor, so the lookup key must be the shell's majority color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/42/code.py:38:#   the fused rule must count the full shell, choose the outer majority color, paint only the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/42/code.py:88:#   would produce a different fill. But both filled sprites consistently use the majority shell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/42/code.py:90:# - The output colors depend only on visible palette entries, visible shell frequencies, and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/42/code.py:489:      a repeated accent color with a different majority shell color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/42/code.py:501:    - The correct color comes from the full multicolor shell, not from the inner accent layer,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/24/code.py:43:  7 -> add diamond shell at radius 4\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/24/code.py:44:  3 -> add diamond shell at radii 5..6\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/24/code.py:47:  result: a diamond output with outer shells 7 and 3, and an enlarged inner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/24/code.py:249:    - later stripes add outer diamond shells of matching thickness\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3e6067c3/21/code.py:61:# - 假设每个目标对象都是单色矩形环包围单色实心矩形；`_draw_frame()` 保证这一点。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/3/code.py:24:#   7 with h=1 -> add the radius-2 shell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/3/code.py:25:#   3 with h=2 -> add shells at radii 3 and 4\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/3/code.py:74:# - The output contains only one nested structure, with one color per radial\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/3/code.py:90:# - main() assumes the intended object is centered and uses Manhattan shells;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/40/code.py:57:#     - The original fill step assumed adjacency colors carry meaning. With multicolor shells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/40/code.py:77:#     - The solver does not group border components at all, so multicolor shells cannot break it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/40/code.py:167:    Key insight: The controlling signal is the size of the empty interior, while the multicolor shell is only a distraction layer left unchanged in the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/40/code.py:200:    \"\"\"Paint a validated shell with a strict-majority main color plus accent noise.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3e6067c3/22/code.py:33:     并逐色找矩形环组件.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3e6067c3/22/code.py:66:   - `_detect_frames()` 假设每个有效对象都是单色矩形环包围单色实心矩形; `_draw_frame()` 保证.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/19/code.py:47:- every visible shell is exactly 1 pixel thick\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/19/code.py:71:- Filling a whole shell with one color no longer holds because D12 requires some\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:16:# - Keep the original edge palette: a 2xN or Nx2 legend maps shell-border colors to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:19:#   1. a large mapped hollow shell,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:20:#   2. a smaller mapped hollow shell nested inside the large shell,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:21:#   3. a separate witness shell outside the large shell that reuses the nested shell's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:23:# - The witness shell shows the normal palette mapping for the small-shell color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:24:#   Inside the large shell, the nested shell would also map to that small color if it\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:25:#   were processed alone, but the new D9 rule says shells are handled from smaller area\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:28:#   1. process the nested shell first: its inner hole gets the small shell's mapped\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:30:#   2. process the external witness shell: its hole gets the same mapped fill and keeps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:31:#      it because no larger shell contains it;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:32:#   3. process the outer shell last: its interior is defined relative only to its own\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:33:#      border, so it paints the annulus and the nested shell's inner hole, overwriting\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:34:#      that earlier small-shell fill while leaving shell borders untouched.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:37:#   border. The fused task instead lets multiple shells target overlapping interior\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:38:#   cells, so ordering by visible shell size becomes part of the rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:41:# - The layout uses exactly one nested pair plus one external witness shell. That is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:43:# - Only two mapped shell colors are behaviorally active in the play area. Extra palette\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:45:# - The nested small shell and the witness shell share the same border color. This gives\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:46:#   repeated evidence for the small shell's palette mapping while still allowing the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:47:#   nested instance to be visually overwritten by the larger shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:51:#   a later larger shell may repaint cells that were already filled by a smaller shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:53:#   ownership regions.\" In the fused rule, each shell defines its own inside region\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:54:#   independently; nested borders do not stop a larger shell from repainting through the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:57:#   The new solver must derive all shell masks from the immutable input snapshot and only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:65:#   shells from the frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:68:# - The nested shell is placed with a visible bg annulus around it. The witness shell is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:69:#   separated from the large shell by one empty row, so it never merges with it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:72:# - Every sample contains one same-colored witness shell outside the nest. This makes the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:73:#   small-shell palette mapping visible in the output, so the nested overwrite is not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:75:# - The large shell's final fill visibly occupies both the annulus and the nested hole,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:76:#   while the nested shell border still remains visible. That makes the overwrite effect\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:80:# - The play area uses three shells with simple rectangular outlines. No extra markers,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:82:# - The nested region is concentrated in one upper block and the witness shell sits in a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:87:#   the only ordering signal is visible shell area.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:88:# - Because the nested shell and the witness shell share a border color, the solver can\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:90:#   the large shell's fill due to later overwrite rather than due to a different mapping.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:93:# - The solver assumes each shell border is a single 4-connected component. The generator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:95:# - The solver assumes shell areas for the semantically active components are strictly\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:97:# - The solver assumes repaintable interior cells are exactly \"inside a shell while not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:98:#   belonging to any shell border or the palette.\" The generator constructs only ring\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:282:    \"\"\"Connected monochrome shell components outside the palette.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:319:def _inside_mask_for_shell(blocked: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:321:    Cells enclosed by one shell if that shell alone is treated as a wall.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:323:    All non-shell cells, including other sprite borders, remain traversable during this\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:324:    reachability test. This is what allows larger shells to repaint nested interiors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:352:def _fill_area_sorted_shells(base: np.ndarray, bg: int, mapping: dict[int, int], pal_mask: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:354:    Fill each mapped shell from smaller area to larger area.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:356:    Later shells overwrite earlier fills wherever their independent interior masks\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:357:    overlap, but shell-border cells themselves are never recolored.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:367:        inside = _inside_mask_for_shell(comp[\"mask\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:376:    Fill hollow shells using an edge palette, but resolve nested cases by area-ordered overwrite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:380:    - The play area contains hollow single-color shells, including a small shell nested inside a larger shell and a separate witness shell of the same small-shell color elsewhere.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:384:    - Treat each shell independently: the cells inside a shell are those that cannot reach the grid boundary if only that shell border is considered a wall.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:385:    - Process mapped shells from smaller visible area to larger visible area, painting their interior cells while leaving all shell borders unchanged. Later larger shells may overwrite fills written earlier by smaller nested shells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:388:    - Nested shell borders do not partition the final answer into fixed ownership regions. The decisive clue is that shells are applied in area order, so a large enclosing shell can repaint a nested shell's earlier fill even though the nested shell would map to a different palette color on its own.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:394:    return _fill_area_sorted_shells(g, bg, mapping, pal_mask)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/21/code.py:465:    \"\"\"Choose palette entries plus distinct outer/inner mapped shell colors.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/800d221b/18/code.py:48:#     rectangle, the frame is a one-pixel shell, and the branch is the external chain. This keeps the grid legible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:16:# - Keep the edge palette mechanic: a 2xN or Nx2 legend on the frame maps shell-border\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:19:#   stack: one large outer shell contains one broken middle shell, and that middle shell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:20:#   contains one tiny inner shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:21:# - The middle shell has a deliberate gap, so its cavity merges into the large shell's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:25:#      middle shell as \"its hole\" because the middle shell visually surrounds that area.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:26:#   2. The combo solver instead checks edge reachability. Because the middle shell has a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:27:#      gap, that space can escape into the outer cavity, so it is not the middle shell's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:29:#   3. The merged region is owned by the outer shell, while the tiny inner hole is still\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:30:#      owned by the tiny shell because that one remains closed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:33:# - The generator uses one clean three-level nested structure instead of many unrelated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:36:#   broken middle shell plus one closed tiny shell. That is enough to expose the D8 change\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:44:# - The original logic also assumes a hole belongs to the shell that merely touches it most.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:45:#   In the combo task, ownership depends on which shell disconnects the region from the grid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:47:# - The original in-place update pattern is risky once shells are nested, because a later\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:55:#   separate and cannot be mistaken for part of a shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:56:# - The outer shell is always at least one cell away from the global frame, guaranteeing that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:58:# - The middle shell fits strictly inside the outer shell with a bg moat on all sides.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:59:# - The tiny inner shell fits strictly inside the middle shell's main cavity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:61:#   annulus but the tiny shell remains isolated inside that merged region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:64:# - Every sample contains at least one bg region that touches multiple mapped shell colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:65:#   This makes the \"pick the true enclosing shell\" signal visible in the I/O pairs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:67:#   interior once the gap appears, even though it still sits inside the large shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:72:# - The play area only contains four semantic objects: the palette, the outer shell, the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:73:#   middle shell with one tail/bar, and the tiny inner shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:74:# - All shells are simple ring-like shapes. No extra markers, text, or scattered distractors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:80:# - Only three shell colors are active in the nested structure, which keeps the examples\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:83:#   palette mapping applies, but the owning shell changes with topology.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:86:# - `_select_region_border` assumes each relevant shell is one connected non-bg component.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:87:#   The generator builds each shell as exactly one connected component.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:92:#   parent shell the smallest enclosing adjacent shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:93:# - The solver assumes the palette is isolated from shells by at least one cell so palette\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:375:    \"\"\"Count mapped adjacent shell colors and collect adjacent component ids.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:416:    A mapped shell owns the region if, when that shell alone is treated as a wall,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:417:    the region cannot reach the grid edge. This handles nested shells and shells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:418:    with gaps. If no enclosing mapped shell is found, fall back to dominant mapped\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:443:    \"\"\"List interior bg regions with their owning shell color (or None).\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:473:    \"\"\"Fill all interior bg regions according to their owning enclosing shell.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:485:    Fill interiors of nested hollow shells using an edge legend, with topology-aware ownership.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:489:    - The main object area contains a large hollow shell, a smaller broken shell nested inside\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:490:      it, and a tiny closed shell nested inside that smaller shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:496:    - For each candidate interior region, choose the adjacent shell that truly disconnects that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:497:      region from the grid edge, then fill the region with that shell's mapped color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:500:    - In nested layouts, a bg region can touch several shell colors, so the most frequent\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:501:      neighboring color is not necessarily the owner. The correct owner is the shell whose wall\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:557:    \"\"\"Pick palette keys/fills and assign three distinct mapped shell colors.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:563:    shell_colors = rng.sample(border_keys, 3)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:564:    outer_color, middle_color, inner_color = map(int, shell_colors)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:603:    Build the nested middle shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:605:    The 7x7 shell is deliberately broken at the top center so its cavity merges with the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/13/code.py:620:    \"\"\"Small closed shell with a 1-cell hole.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/18/code.py:70:     missing-head, and empty-shell. Real movers still display the original\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:28:#      the full connected shell touching a hole, not the most frequent color adjacent to that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:35:#        matched sprite: full shell counts {2: 7, 4: 5}, hole-adjacent counts {4: 5, 2: 3}.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:38:#        unmatched sprite: full shell counts {8: 7, 2: 5}, hole-adjacent counts {2: 5, 8: 3}.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:39:#        Old task logic would fill via key 2. Combo logic sees shell-majority 8, finds no key 8,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:50:#      identified the sprite. This breaks once the shell is multicolor, so the solver must first\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:65:#      multicolor shells, at least one disappearing shell, and at least one palette entry that is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:68:#      the original \"nearest-border color\" heuristic and force full-shell majority reasoning.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:70:#    - Objects are separated by background and use simple one-hole ring-like shapes, so the shell,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:77:#      \"shell majority color appears on the palette key side\" rather than any hidden numeric rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:304:    Fill matched holes by shell-majority key; delete unmatched touching shells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:326:        shell_counts: Counter[int] = Counter()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:328:            shell_counts.update(comp_counts[cid])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:329:        border_key = int(shell_counts.most_common(1)[0][0])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:351:    - Hollow sprites are separated from the palette, but each sprite shell may mix two border colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:356:    - Find enclosed background regions away from the palette, then identify the full connected shell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:358:    - Use the shell's most frequent color as the lookup key. If that majority color is in the palette,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:361:    Key insight: The palette does two jobs at once, but both are driven by whole-shell majority color:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:490:    \"\"\"Return per-hole touching shell cells, their union, and all shell cells.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:508:    Color a shell so the accent dominates around the hole but the major dominates globally.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:527:    shell_counts = Counter(int(sprite[r, c]) for r, c in border_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:529:    if shell_counts.most_common(1)[0][0] != int(major_color):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:537:    \"\"\"Render a multicolor shell and optionally fill its hole.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:645:    # - unused palette keys must stay absent from every sprite shell,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:659:    seen_shell_colors = set(int(v) for v in non_palette_cells[(non_palette_cells != bg) & (~pal_mask)])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/23/code.py:660:    if any(int(k) in seen_shell_colors for k in unused_keys):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/8/code.py:92:    \"\"\"Keep only the 4-neighbor outer shell of a binary sprite mask.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/6/code.py:31:#      the hole-adjacent shell cells may contain accent=4 and major=2 in a 4:2 split,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/6/code.py:32:#      while the full shell contains major=2 and accent=4 in an 8:4 split.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/6/code.py:37:#      whole shell before the stripe writer runs, otherwise the wrong palette key is chosen.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/6/code.py:40:#      majority\" visible without turning shells into noise.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/6/code.py:49:#      That fails for multicolor shells, so the solver now labels full non-palette\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/6/code.py:58:#    - The multicolor border constructor guarantees `major` is the strict whole-shell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/6/code.py:61:#    - Humans can inspect the full shell and see that the repeated border color, not the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/6/code.py:298:    \"\"\"Group multicolor sprite cells into connected shells and count their colors.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/6/code.py:312:    Fill each enclosed hole by using the touching shell's majority color as the palette key,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/6/code.py:331:        shell_counts: Counter[int] = Counter()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/6/code.py:333:            shell_counts.update(comp_counts[cid])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/6/code.py:334:        border_key = int(shell_counts.most_common(1)[0][0])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/6/code.py:347:    - Hollow sprites sit away from that legend; each sprite shell may mix multiple border colors instead of staying monochrome.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/6/code.py:352:    - For every hole, gather the whole touching shell, choose the shell's most frequent border color as the lookup key, read the mapped fill color from the palette, and paint the hole with alternating stripes of that fill color and the background. Wider-or-square holes use vertical stripes; taller holes use horizontal stripes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/6/code.py:355:    - The color decision and the painting pattern are controlled by different visible cues: the shell's global majority color chooses the palette entry, while the hole's own geometry chooses whether the mapped color alternates by column or by row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/6/code.py:399:    Create a one-hole shell with slight irregularity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/6/code.py:513:    \"\"\"Return shell cells touching holes, their union, and the full shell set.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/6/code.py:533:    Color a shell so the hole-adjacent cells prefer `accent_color` locally but the full shell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/6/code.py:579:    \"\"\"Render a multicolor shell and optionally stripe its hole.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c3d4a41/29/code.py:65:#    - The frame keeps the original 8x11 shell, so the output core still fits entirely inside the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/29/code.py:63:#   inner bg region when converted into a shell ring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/26/code.py:131:def _detect_shell_insets(mask: np.ndarray) -> tuple[list[int], np.ndarray]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/26/code.py:169:    insets, _cropped = _detect_shell_insets(g == int(color))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/26/code.py:173:def _shells_for_color(g: np.ndarray, color: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/26/code.py:180:    insets, cropped = _detect_shell_insets(mask)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/26/code.py:184:    shell_mask = np.zeros_like(cropped, dtype=bool)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/26/code.py:186:        _paint_square_border(shell_mask, int(inset))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/26/code.py:189:    out[r0 : r1 + 1, c0 : c1 + 1] = shell_mask\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/26/code.py:200:    above: dict[int, set[int]] = {color: set() for color, _layers, _shells in group}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/26/code.py:201:    indegree: dict[int, int] = {color: 0 for color, _layers, _shells in group}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/26/code.py:241:    - Drawings may overlap, but every true shell keeps enough visible perimeter to remain detectable inside a square bbox.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/26/code.py:245:    - The number of detected shells is that color's layer count; the unique color with zero shells is the padding/noise color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/26/code.py:246:    - Order real colors by layer count in descending order, breaking ties by bottom-to-top cover order among overlapping reconstructed shell masks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/26/code.py:259:        shells = _shells_for_color(g, int(color))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/26/code.py:260:        counts.append((int(color), int(layers), shells))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/26/code.py:262:    drawings = [(color, layers, shells) for color, layers, shells in counts if layers > 0]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/26/code.py:263:    pad_colors = [color for color, layers, _shells in counts if layers == 0]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca