 从左侧支路进入，3 个目标挂在环的其它支路上。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/35/code.py:30:#    - 环结构固定为一个粗矩形环加 4 条短支路，自由度适中，生成成功率高且视觉稳定。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:14:  - yellow pixels do not travel through the whole floor; they stay on the 1-cell boundary shell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:22:    there is a green obstacle mass. The black passable cells form only a thin shell around that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:23:    obstacle. The yellow moves around corners on that shell and stacks near the terminal end of the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:24:    shell after the cycle is cut at the shell cell closest to the legend corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:27:    the shell long and winding.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:44:    movers are restricted to its passable shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:53:room is exactly `obstacle_core ∪ 1-cell shell`, so the room contour equals the yellow movement\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:59:  - define the passable shell as the 4-neighbor exterior of that core\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:60:  - define the room as `core ∪ shell`\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:64:cores whose shell is not a single simple cycle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:73:The generator rejects simple rectangle-like shells, so examples visibly depend on the obstacle\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:78:obstacles, yellow movers. The passable shell is one cell thick, so the motion path is readable and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:97:  - every accepted sample contains at least one obstacle-shaped shell that is non-rectangular, so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:345:    Slide yellow pixels inside obstacle-filled rooms along the ordered boundary shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:349:    - Every movable region is a bounded meta-component made of black shell cells, yellow movers,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:351:    - The passable shell is a one-cell lane wrapped between the colored outer wall and the green\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:360:    - Yellow pixels slide forward on that contour shell and stack at the far end; obstacle and wall\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:364:    - Obstacles change the room contour itself, so the true movement path is the shell created by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:510:def _shape_has_simple_shell(room: set[tuple[int, int]], corner: str, clockwise: bool, h: int, w: int) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/21/code.py:569:        if not _shape_has_simple_shell(room, corner, clockwise, h, w):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/36/code.py:30:#   shell depth, and the ordering direction flips from ascending to descending.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/36/code.py:52:#   clipping, and fully visible shells for every color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/36/code.py:66:#   \"count same-color square shells, keep that color, sort by count descending\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/36/code.py:70:#   gaps between shells, and validates that the descending output differs from both the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/36/code.py:77:# - Every shell perimeter is fully present, so exact square-border detection is valid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/36/code.py:107:def _detect_shell_insets(mask: np.ndarray) -> tuple[list[int], tuple[int, int, int, int] | None]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/36/code.py:138:    insets, b = _detect_shell_insets(g == int(color))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/36/code.py:153:    - That shell count is the object's value.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/36/code.py:154:    - Sort the objects by shell count in descending order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/89565ca0/36/code.py:158:    - The value is now written directly into the picture as the number of concentric square shells, so there is no need to reconstruct rooms or identify a separate pad color. The only nontrivial step is reading shell depth and reversing the old sort direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/34/code.py:27:  preserved_shell:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:259:      monochromatic parts: a large outer shell and a small inner part with a different color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:260:    - Two distant sprites reuse the same shell color, so one foreground color appears in two disconnected places.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:379:    shell_color, accent_color = colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:389:        shell_mask = np.zeros((h, w), dtype=bool)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:390:        shell_mask[0, :] = True\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:391:        shell_mask[-1, :] = True\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:392:        shell_mask[:, 0] = True\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:393:        shell_mask[:, -1] = True\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:403:        if np.any(shell_mask & accent_mask):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:406:        sprite[shell_mask] = shell_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:416:            \"shell_mask_local\": shell_mask,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:438:        shell_mask = np.zeros((GRID_SIZE, GRID_SIZE), dtype=bool)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:440:        shell_local = spec[\"shell_mask_local\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:442:        shell_mask[r0 : r0 + h, c0 : c0 + w] = shell_local\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:453:        spec[\"shell_mask\"] = shell_mask\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:457:        spec[\"union_coords\"] = [tuple(x) for x in np.argwhere(shell_mask | accent_mask)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:515:    shell_color, accent_color = spec[\"colors\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:523:    shell_noise_target = random.randint(0, 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:547:    for _ in range(shell_noise_target):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:549:            spec[\"shell_mask\"],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:554:            shell_color,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:562:        chosen.append((r, c, shell_color))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:582:    shared_shell = fg[0]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:583:    unique_shell = fg[1]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:586:    shell_colors = [shared_shell, shared_shell, unique_shell]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:587:    random.shuffle(shell_colors)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/15/code.py:588:    pairs = [(shell_colors[i], accent_colors[i]) for i in range(NUM_SPRITES)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/26/code.py:3:# Name: 凸出方向源消失\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f931b4a8/8/code.py:52:#    - 框架层数固定为少量、规则的矩形环，避免散点噪声；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/11/code.py:3:# Name: C4旋转对称+同心矩形环纹理\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/25/code.py:18:#      3. D6/0: do not delete the whole src object; keep its outline shell visible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/25/code.py:32:#      into a shell. This is much easier to infer than a large family of unrelated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/25/code.py:41:#      visibly show the emptied source shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/25/code.py:54:#      could hide the source-shell effect. The generator therefore places the cropped\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/25/code.py:67:#      change, and src/dst are bbox-separated so the shell/fill contrast remains clear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/25/code.py:299:    the src colored subsprites so its outline remains as an empty shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/25/code.py:689:    src_shell, _ = _render_object(layout, src_shapes, colors, bg, outline_col, filled=False)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/25/code.py:690:    if src_shell is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/25/code.py:692:    if not _is_8connected(src_shell, bg):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/25/code.py:694:    if _count_enclosed_bg_holes(src_shell, bg) != n_cavities:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/25/code.py:696:    if src_shell.shape != src_filled.shape:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/25/code.py:698:    if int(np.count_nonzero(src_filled != bg)) <= int(np.count_nonzero(src_shell != bg)):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/25/code.py:701:    return src_filled, src_shell, dst_empty, dst_filled\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/25/code.py:794:    src_filled, src_shell, dst_empty, dst_filled = built\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/25/code.py:796:    placed = _place_on_canvas(src_filled, src_shell, dst_empty, dst_filled, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/8/code.py:97:#      the nested structure remains readable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/8/code.py:100:#    - The nested structure gives a strong structural cue for \"outer layer,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:18:#    - stage 1 marker: a thick outer cross shell in color 8,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:22:#    - fused: the visible input contains a plus-shaped azure shell with a smaller black plus inside it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:23:#      First recover the shell while treating both colors as hidden; this exposes clean witnesses needed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:26:#      on a witness that initially sits under the outer shell, so the second pass is genuinely downstream\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:32:#    because the shell is a real cross silhouette, not a barely perturbed rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:44:#    - stage 1 treats the whole outer cross footprint (shell + inner cross) as hidden,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:61:#    - color 8 appears exactly on the outer-shell cells of one thick cross,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:219:    - The occluder is now a concentric two-layer cross: a thick outer shell in color 8 surrounds a thinner inner cross in color 0.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:223:    - Detect the nested outer-shell/inner-core cross pair and infer the reflected strip start while ignoring both marker colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:224:    - First restore every outer-shell cell from its reflection orbit, falling back to the transpose witness only when the full orbit is hidden.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:229:    input because all of their non-inner orbit witnesses are still sitting under the outer shell, so the outer layer has to be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:238:    shell = outer_full & ~inner_full\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:241:    for r, c in np.argwhere(shell):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2b83f449/19/code.py:8:# - Keep the original geometry shell: even rows are pipe rows, odd rows are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/33/code.py:25:# - 嵌套形状只采样两类视觉清晰、对齐稳定的模板：矩形环与菱形环。这样“同色双环”在 2-4 个样例中很容易被观察到，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/19/code.py:17:#    radial shell (outside to inside) plus clockwise quadrant order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/19/code.py:32:#      essential distinction is shell + clockwise phase, not lexicographic position.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/19/code.py:40:#    The quartets are placed in four quadrants and repeated on two shells, so the rotational\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/19/code.py:42:#    contains two shells, and the generator rejects cases where the old row/col rule would\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/19/code.py:67:    - Both objects use a C4-symmetric cavity arrangement: two shells of four quadrants each.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/19/code.py:69:      outer shell first, clockwise UL->UR->LR->LL, then the next inner shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头形精灵凸出方向\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/23/code.py:32:#      because the inner outline islands are disconnected from the outer shell when the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/25/code.py:271:      border-colored shells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/25/code.py:341:    \"\"\"Build a square sprite shell with exactly `hole_count` 4-connected bg holes.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/12/code.py:74:#   fresh visible cells, so the nested structure stays readable instead of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/3/code.py:23:#    重复涂成矩形环。这里两处同时改动：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/7/code.py:18:#   whole region was painted by boundary shell number. Example: if a rectangular\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/7/code.py:20:#   palette[boundary_dist % 3], so the outer border was A and shells moved inward.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/7/code.py:181:    The marker chain no longer encodes boundary shells. Instead it shows the first\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/8/code.py:23:#      source object is a 3-color nested sprite (outer shell, middle band, core). Example:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/1/code.py:20:#      nested fill colors: outer shell, middle ring, and smallest core.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/1/code.py:38:#      pasted opaquely, so the outer shell becomes a visible bg moat cut out of the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/1/code.py:52:#      different core colors, so the old \"look at the dominant shell\" heuristic fails\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/1/code.py:222:    - The top region contains separated three-color sprites: one outer shell touching\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/1/code.py:229:    - Recolor layerwise on the docked copy: outer shell -> bg, middle band -> target\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/1/code.py:234:    - The decisive cue is the least-area inner core, and the outer shell does not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/1/code.py:401:    smallest core color instead of the dominant shell or the middle ring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:23:#     preserve the outer shell, bbox, and scale\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:26:#       1. shell layer contour\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:33:#     [shell A + inner A] -> [shell A + inner B]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:34:#     [shell B + inner B] -> [shell B + inner A]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:38:#       [shell A + inner A]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:39:#         -> [shell A + inner B]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:40:#         -> [shell A contour stays A] + [inner A contour sits on top of inner B]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:41:#     because the shell is preserved, its contour is mostly semantically important;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:46:#   why not reuse the 5x5 shell / 3x3 inner layout from the single D4 variant:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:52:#     enlarge only enough to a 6x6 shell with a 4x4 inner chamber; this keeps scale-1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:55:#   why keep exactly 2 shell groups and 2 inner prototypes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:62:#     combo status: false; only the inner layer is swapped, so solver must parse shell vs inner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:65:#     combo status: false; that would miss the inner-layer boundary because shell and inner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:69:#     combo status: unnecessary; every sprite is an exact scaled 6x6 box and the shell is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:73:#     combo status: true, but generator must ensure both shell-color groups appear at scale 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:77:#     shell colors must be distinct and readable from visible border cells such as arr[0, 0]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:83:#   input and output patches share the same bbox because the shell is preserved and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:94:#     shell colors stay with their groups, but the content inside each shell changes to the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:97:#     humans can match shells by outer color, see that the inner motif came from the other\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:98:#     shell group, and also notice that only the inner edge preserves old colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:105:#   shell colors define the two groups perceptually\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:111:#     the smallest-scale sprites include one exemplar from each shell-color group\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:229:    \"\"\"Contour union of the shell layer and the inner layer, each measured separately.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:233:    shell = np.full_like(arr, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:234:    shell[:scale, :] = arr[:scale, :]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:235:    shell[-scale:, :] = arr[-scale:, :]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:236:    shell[:, :scale] = arr[:, :scale]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:237:    shell[:, -scale:] = arr[:, -scale:]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:242:    return _edge_mask(shell, bg) | _edge_mask(inner, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:304:    Swap the inner nested motif between the two shell groups and keep source-colored layer rims.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:312:    - For each sprite, keep its outer shell, bbox, and scale fixed, but replace the inner 4x4 pattern with the other group's inner pattern.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:313:    - After the inner swap, repaint the 1-pixel contour of the source shell layer and the 1-pixel contour of the source inner layer at their original cells using their original colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/12/code.py:316:    - The fused task cannot be solved by treating the sprite as one flat blob. The solver must split each object into semantic layers, swap only the contained inner motif, and compute residue on each layer separately so the old inner rim survives inside the unchanged shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/16/code.py:32:      原代码不要求区域必须是矩形，只要求非墙区域是 4 连通块。矩形环带满足这一点，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/11/code.py:21:#      fill colors: outer shell, middle band, and core. The sprite silhouette is not a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/11/code.py:78:#      outer shells plus centered middle/core rectangles to guarantee this.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/11/code.py:219:    - Top area contains separated three-color sprites: one outer shell plus two nested inner layers, all using bar fill colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/9/code.py:10:#   同时存在的矩形环带。若某环带的 marker 距该环带边界深度为 0,1，则填色会从内外两侧同时向中间收缩。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/7/code.py:27:#    bar border recolors the shell, and bar fill is both the inner recolor and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/7/code.py:49:#    selects the bar because the trail and the original shell use that same fill\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/7/code.py:50:#    color, while the docked shell switches to the bar border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/7/code.py:269:    - The upper region contains connected two-color sprites whose shell color matches one bar fill.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/7/code.py:276:    - Dock it at the same x-position, bottom-aligned in that bar, recoloring shell -> bar border\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/33/code.py:17:#      one closed rectangular shell containing a seed blob.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/33/code.py:18:#    - Exactly one shell side is 1 cell thick; the other three sides are 2 or 3\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/33/code.py:31:#        4. Extend the orthogonal shell borders alongside that beam in wall\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/33/code.py:40:#    - The shape family is restricted to axis-aligned shells with four possible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/33/code.py:61:#    - The shell is rendered as a rectangle ring with one thin side and three\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/33/code.py:65:#    - Obstacles are placed only on background cells outside the shell, away\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/33/code.py:77:#        wall color = shell + pipe border,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/33/code.py:85:#      one shell and places the seed inside it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/33/code.py:409:    - The dominant color is background. The most frequent non-background color is one closed rectangular shell around a cavity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/33/code.py:410:    - A smaller non-wall color blob sits inside that cavity. Exactly one shell side is 1 cell thick, while the other three sides are thicker. Any further non-background pixels are outside obstacles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/33/code.py:414:    - Extend the shell's side borders along the beam in wall color so the beam is visibly enclosed inside a pipe.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/33/code.py:518:def _render_shell(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/33/code.py:629:    wall_mask, interior = _render_shell(grid, r0, c0, inner_h, inner_w, thicknesses, wall_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/10/code.py:35:#    like ABAB... on rectangular shells. The fused variant changes three linked\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/10/code.py:37:#    - depth is now Manhattan distance to the region boundary, so the shells are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/10/code.py:85:#    blank rings, and deeper surviving layers keep colors for two shells each.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/10/code.py:236:    The markers simultaneously define palette order, reveal that depth is measured in taxicab shells rather than Chebyshev shells, and punch out their own layers, leaving repeated two-layer diamond bands interrupted by blank gaps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/16/code.py:22:#    common outer shell while moving the discriminative key to the inner color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/16/code.py:30:#    its border-colored shell plus fill-colored core unchanged in the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/16/code.py:58:#    shell, so a solver cannot use that color to distinguish destinations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/16/code.py:71:#    recoloring: shared border color = common shell, unique bar fills = routing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/16/code.py:182:      shell in that shared border color plus a minority inner block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/16/code.py:185:    - First verify the D2-style outer/border agreement: the sprite outer shell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/16/code.py:195:    sprite has the shared border color as its outer shell. Once that condition\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/13/code.py:20:#    The original task treated each region as boundary shells. If a rectangular\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/13/code.py:22:#    that order and repeated it inward on every shell. The fused variant flips\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/12/code.py:19:#     是围绕房间边界向内收缩的矩形环带。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/9/code.py:18:#    - D6/3 replaces that visible opening with a sealed shell. The solver must\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/9/code.py:23:#      1. Input shows a closed rectangular shell with one thin side and three\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/9/code.py:36:#    - The wall family is restricted to one axis-aligned shell with exactly four\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/9/code.py:42:#      repeats the crucial signal twice: thin-side comparison inside the shell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/9/code.py:57:#    - The generator builds one rectangular shell from an outer box minus an\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/9/code.py:254:    # - The chosen wall component is one sealed shell nearest to the seed blob.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/9/code.py:297:    assert not _touches_border(interior), \"closed shell leaked to border\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/9/code.py:364:    - The background is the dominant color, and the most common non-background color is one closed wall shell around a cavity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/9/code.py:508:def _render_shell(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/9/code.py:619:    wall_mask, interior = _render_shell(grid, bg, r0, c0, inner_h, inner_w, t, wall_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/8/code.py:254:def _diamond_shell(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/8/code.py:260:    shell: set[tuple[int, int]] = set()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/8/code.py:265:                shell.add((rr, cc))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/8/code.py:266:    return shell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/8/code.py:316:        \"forbidden_shell\": frozenset(_diamond_shell((h, w), diamond, segment_cells)),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/8/code.py:344:            shell = set(placement[\"forbidden_shell\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/8/code.py:349:            if not occupied.isdisjoint(shell):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/8/code.py:352:            for cell in shell:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/8/code.py:358:            for cell in shell:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/35/code.py:385:    - Color still tells you which motif carves which block, but position is no longer a rectangular pack order. The four-quadrant source scene hides a corner-plus-center nested structure that must be restored in the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/11/code.py:292:def _diamond_shell(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/11/code.py:299:    shell: set[tuple[int, int]] = set()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/11/code.py:303:                shell.add((rr, cc))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/11/code.py:304:    return shell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/11/code.py:398:    shell = _diamond_shell((h, w), diamond, allowed_adjacent)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/11/code.py:399:    if not guard_cells.isdisjoint(shell):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/11/code.py:408:        \"shell\": frozenset(shell),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/11/code.py:437:    blocked_shell: set[tuple[int, int]] = set()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/11/code.py:447:            if not blocked_shell.isdisjoint(placement[\"all_cells\"]):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/11/code.py:449:            if not occupied_all.isdisjoint(placement[\"shell\"]):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/11/code.py:454:            blocked_shell.update(placement[\"shell\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/11/code.py:460:            blocked_shell.difference_update(placement[\"shell\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/9/code.py:80:#    - The samples visibly differ from the output because input holes contain thin hollow shells,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/19/code.py:18:#    The nested structure must be obvious without becoming noisy on a small board, so the generator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/19/code.py:79:    15: {\"h\": (3, 3), \"w\": (3, 3), \"shell\": (3, 3)},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/19/code.py:80:    20: {\"h\": (4, 5), \"w\": (4, 5), \"shell\": (2, 3)},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/19/code.py:458:    shell_r = random.randint(*cfg[\"shell\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/19/code.py:459:    shell_c = random.randint(*cfg[\"shell\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/19/code.py:461:    th = ih + 2 * shell_r + 2 * MOAT_GAP\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/19/code.py:462:    tw = iw + 2 * shell_c + 2 * MOAT_GAP\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/19/code.py:463:    inner_r0 = shell_r + MOAT_GAP\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/19/code.py:464:    inner_c0 = shell_c + MOAT_GAP\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:25:#      depth 1,3,5,...  -> checkerboard shell anchored to the seed parity\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:45:#      because odd-depth checker shells intentionally contain background cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:47:#      shell coloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:65:#    - the activation now forms inward shells instead of a solid blob,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:66:#    - every second shell contains a checkerboard rather than a flat color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:73:#    shell/checker structure only affects previously fillable background cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:74:#    Generator thresholds require both solid shells and checker shells to be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:81:#    The distinction comes from structure: even-depth shells are solid fill,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:82:#    odd-depth shells expose a parity checkerboard.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:86:#      Generator enforces a minimum max depth and minimum odd/even shell counts.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:199:            \"odd_shell_mask\": empty,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:329:    odd_shell_mask = region_bg & ((dist % 2) == 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:335:    odd_checker_fill_mask = odd_shell_mask & checker_phase\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:336:    odd_checker_bg_mask = odd_shell_mask & ~checker_phase\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:349:        \"odd_shell_mask\": odd_shell_mask,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:359:    \"\"\"Quantify whether generated examples exhibit the fused shell+checker behavior.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:367:    odd_total = int(state[\"odd_shell_mask\"].sum())\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:373:        \"odd_shell_cells\": odd_total,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:387:    Fill the wall-bounded reachable region with concentric shells whose odd layers become checkerboard bands.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:395:    - Recolor that final region by boundary depth. Background cells on even-depth shells become solid seed color; background cells on odd-depth shells use a seed-anchored checkerboard of seed color and background color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:397:    Key insight: Geometry is still solved exactly like the original puzzle, but coloring now depends on two overlaid structures at once: concentric boundary-depth shells and a global checker parity for every odd shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:642:    \"\"\"Single attempt to generate a valid input grid for the fused shell-checker variant.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/12/code.py:710:    if metrics[\"odd_shell_cells\"] < MIN_ODD_SHELL_CELLS:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/12/code.py:32:#    scale, and the original positions are still marked by gray shells. The relation between\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/27/code.py:19:#      a second tool whose enclosing shell has 13 cells around a 1x3 inner bar.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/27/code.py:33:#    inner core rather than the enclosing shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/27/code.py:46:#    - The inserted color is not the exposed shell; it is the enclosed inner core.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/27/code.py:62:#    A human can see two repeated motifs: detached tools are nested shells around\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/27/code.py:65:#    land in the middle and the shells sit around them, making the role swap\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/27/code.py:78:#    visible large shell versus small core.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/27/code.py:287:    shell_mask = mask & (~core_mask)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/27/code.py:288:    assert shell_mask.any()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/27/code.py:291:    shell_colors = sorted({int(x) for x in patch[shell_mask].flatten()})\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/27/code.py:293:    assert len(shell_colors) == 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/27/code.py:294:    assert core_colors[0] != shell_colors[0]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/27/code.py:298:    _shell_lab, shell_n = label(shell_mask, structure=STRUCT4)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/27/code.py:300:    assert shell_n == 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/27/code.py:305:        \"shell_mask\": shell_mask,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/27/code.py:307:        \"outer_color\": int(shell_colors[0]),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/27/code.py:309:        \"outer_count\": int(shell_mask.sum()),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/27/code.py:451:    Dock nested shell-and-core tools back into border sockets.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/27/code.py:472:    the enclosing shell occupies the surrounding rim.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/30/code.py:19:#    - Combo task: the clean scene is a three-layer nested structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/25/code.py:21:#   - Concrete trace: the shell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/25/code.py:38:#   - Real emitters are still 4-connected shells, but at least one shell has an off-wall hole that now\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/25/code.py:200:    - Black marks on the left include true 4-connected shells and diagonal 8-connected decoys over one bg color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/25/code.py:204:    - In the slid left pane, locate every enclosed bg component; each such hole contributes all of its rows, no matter where inside the shell it sits.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/17/code.py:13:# - Small example: a 2x3 inner block of frame color sits inside a 5x4 shell of plug color. In the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/17/code.py:14:#   output, that 2x3 inner block fills the notch exactly; the shell is projected outward from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/17/code.py:26:# - A stricter rigid-body interpretation creates a geometric conflict: a fully surrounding shell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/17/code.py:27:#   cannot be inserted wholesale into a border notch without some shell pixels landing on the frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/17/code.py:29:#   exactly with the cavity, while shell pixels are only kept where the transformed shell lands on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/17/code.py:38:# - The standalone tools visibly show an inner kernel inside an outer shell, so the nesting rule is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/17/code.py:41:# - Only the shell is left visible outside the frame after docking; no extra symbols or hidden\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/17/code.py:45:#   frame/tool color agreement, and a stable \"kernel fills, shell protrudes\" action.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/17/code.py:425:    - The outer shell stays as the visible protrusion outside the notch, and the tool disappears\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/17/code.py:447:        # - at least one outer-shell pixel lands on empty space outside the frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/31/code.py:9:#    - D16/2 adds filled-hole distractors: some closed shells contain a non-background color inside the cavity. Those colored cavities move\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/31/code.py:10:#      together with the shell, but they are inert and must never emit.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/31/code.py:14:#        * a 4x3 rectangular shell with a 2x1 magenta cavity touching `sep-2` emits;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/31/code.py:15:#        * a same-sized shell with a blue 2x1 cavity does not emit because the cavity color is not the background;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/31/code.py:16:#        * a 3x3 shell with a single magenta cavity at `sep-2` does not emit because its area is 1.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/31/code.py:25:#      a colored cavity fill must move with its enclosing shell. The new solver therefore shifts black components and any non-background interior\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/31/code.py:36:#    - Colored cavity fills are only placed strictly inside enclosing shells, never on the shell boundary, so they can be assigned unambiguously\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/31/code.py:39:#    - A human can compare two equally large closed shells near the separator and notice that only the one whose hole looks like background emits.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/31/code.py:49:#    - The solver assumes any non-background colored pixel on the left lies inside the bbox interior of exactly one black shell. The generator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/31/code.py:171:    - Black shells live on the left over one shared background color, and some shells may contain enclosed interior fills whose color is either the background itself or a small non-background distractor color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/31/code.py:174:    - Move each black connected component rightward until its right edge is flush with the separator; any colored fill enclosed inside that shell moves by the same horizontal amount.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/31/code.py:178:    Key insight: being a closed hole next to the separator is no longer sufficient; a cavity must both look like genuine background inside the shell and occupy more than one cell before it behaves like a nozzle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/31/code.py:237:def _rect_shell(hole_h: int, hole_w: int, fill_color: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/31/code.py:335:            patch = _rect_shell(hole_h, hole_w, BG)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/31/code.py:344:            patch = _rect_shell(hole_h, hole_w, fill)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/31/code.py:346:            patch = _rect_shell(1, 1, BG)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/27/code.py:22:#   original-style scene: [emitter irregular shell, distractor C-shape, emitter]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/24/code.py:38:#     - sprite A is a closed shell; after sliding, it has a 1-cell cavity at local col bbox_w-2\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/24/code.py:39:#     - sprite B is an open-top shell; after sliding, its mouth also reaches bbox_w-2\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/33/code.py:26:#   original solved shell: right wall at `sep-1`, hole rows touch `sep-2`, so rows {7,8,9} fire.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/33/code.py:27:#   combo solved shell: right wall stops at `sep-2`, column `sep-1` stays blank, hole rows touch\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/1/code.py:329:    \"\"\"Build an emitter sprite patch: a closed shell with an interior hole at the right edge.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/23/code.py:134:      by the extra 9 shell that appears only after docking.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/23/code.py:479:        shell_abs = set()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/23/code.py:484:                    shell_abs.add(q)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/23/code.py:487:        for rr, cc in list(train_abs) + list(shell_abs):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/23/code.py:503:        for rr, cc in shell_abs:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/23/code.py:878:    shell = _dilate8(body_mask) & (~body_mask) & (~occupied)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/23/code.py:879:    out[shell] = 9\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/3/code.py:31:    - Imagine two closed shells that both become flush with the separator after sliding.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/3/code.py:32:    - In the original task, both shells would emit red because every trigger row was hard-coded red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/3/code.py:33:    - In the fused task, shell A may contain green inside its trigger cavity and shell B may contain\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/3/code.py:40:      the black shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/3/code.py:99:    - Markers appear only inside black shells, not scattered in open background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/4/code.py:22:#   not themselves become shell colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/4/code.py:30:#     D10-only task: A/B/C/D/E all get successive shell colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/4/code.py:31:#     combo task: A/B/C get successive shell colors, while D/E remain azure even\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/4/code.py:43:#   show several shell colors, but small enough that the cap is countable by eye.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/4/code.py:45:#   colored shell layers and also a nontrivial set of still-reachable background\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/4/code.py:58:#   unrestricted chamber flood; only the shell rendering stage is radius-limited.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/4/code.py:74:#   2) the number of outward shell bands from the magenta seed changes with it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/4/code.py:76:#   colored shell, the cap reads as \"flood stops after N steps\", not merely as a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/4/code.py:81:#   radius code, shell colors = distance layers, azure = untouched background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/4/code.py:82:# - Decorations are few and small so they do not overwhelm the shell pattern.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/4/code.py:267:def _unbounded_shell_output(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/4/code.py:283:    - Erase decorative blue fragments stranded behind structural walls, but color only the reachable background cells whose distance is between 1 and N, assigning a fixed shell color to each step.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/4/code.py:286:    - The blue-wall separation still tells you what the chamber is, but the red token count decides how many BFS shells from the magenta seed are actually rendered. Farther chamber cells remain plain background even though the chamber itself continues beyond them.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/4/code.py:488:    unbounded = _unbounded_shell_output(inp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/11/code.py:24:# - Concrete trace: after sliding, suppose one sprite becomes a 5x4 black shell whose interior hole is 3x2\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/11/code.py:37:#     emitters remain closed shells and distractors remain open or solid shapes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/6/code.py:443:    Key insight: Coupler count still chooses the destination and stripe-colored markers still fix orientation, but now the train must be read as a hollow frame whose interior markers are disconnected, whose docked body changes color from the target region, and whose old shell remains behind as a ghost.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/7/code.py:267:def _rect_shell(hole_h: int, hole_w: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/7/code.py:322:    return _rect_shell(1, 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/32/code.py:52:#   This remains valid because every emitter is a closed shell and no distractor openings\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/32/code.py:149:    Read already-aligned black shells beside the grey divider and fire red rays from their sealed outlets.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/32/code.py:157:    - Find enclosed magenta regions inside the black shells; whenever a hole reaches the inner column immediately left of the separator, all rows of that hole become ray rows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/17/code.py:18:#       rear emitter: a closed shell one column farther left\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/17/code.py:19:#       free emitter: another closed shell in a disjoint row band\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/17/code.py:23:#       combo rule: blocker lands first; its wall at sep-1 stops the rear shell at right wall = sep-2,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/17/code.py:24:#       so that shell's hole ends at sep-3 and no longer triggers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/17/code.py:33:#   - The object vocabulary stays small: closed shell emitters, one L-shaped blocker, and at most no\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/17/code.py:56:#   - The blocked shell and the free shell look like the same emitter family, but only the one that can\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/17/code.py:237:    Key insight: The output depends on two coupled effects: motion is no longer simultaneous, so nearer sprites can prevent farther shells from reaching the separator, and even the shells that do trigger collapse their whole cavity into a single central ray.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/17/code.py:261:    \"\"\"Closed shell with a hole that reaches the column just left of the right wall when flush.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/15/code.py:386:    assert sh == 3, f\"emitters are designed as 3-row nozzle shells, got {sh}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/22/code.py:40:#     if a slid right-side shell has a hole spanning rows 7..9 (height 3),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/22/code.py:50:#   distractors, so the puzzle is not reduced to \"every shell emits\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/22/code.py:79:# - The variable that controls the new path, hole height, is directly visible in the black shell and is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/22/code.py:103:#   * emitter patches are simple mirrored shells with one clean separator-facing hole;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/20/code.py:20:#        sprites are miniature shells while the rays become long and salient.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/20/code.py:33:#     across a few examples: tiny shells repeat on the left, while long cropped rays\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/20/code.py:245:    \"\"\"Choose non-adjacent internal divider rows for a tiny emitter shell.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/20/code.py:261:    \"\"\"Build a 3-column closed shell whose cavity lands on sep-2 when flush.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/6/code.py:403:def _colorize_shell(mask: np.ndarray, side: str, seq: tuple[int, int, int], bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/6/code.py:431:        left_shell = _colorize_shell(left_mask, \"left\", seq, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/6/code.py:447:            side_shell = _orient_from_left(left_shell, side)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/6/code.py:450:            arr = side_shell.copy()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/29/code.py:9:      common_shell:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/14/code.py:23:#   typical input therefore shows one shell-like object somewhere left of the separator.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/14/code.py:35:#   is a plain shell or a split shell all vary. The right-side red pattern also varies by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/14/code.py:51:#   only closed-shell emitter shapes, so the triggering cavity is always a true enclosed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/14/code.py:134:    Key insight: With only one sprite and no distractors, the puzzle reduces to the essential causal chain: move the shell to the wall, inspect which rows belong to the sealed cavity touching that wall, and copy those rows as rightward red beams.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/14/code.py:212:    \"\"\"Fill patch with a connected split-shell emitter that still has one triggering cavity.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/14/code.py:239:    \"\"\"Build the single sprite: always one connected closed-shell emitter.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:15:#    - Base task: monochrome black shells slide right until flush with the grey separator;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:18:#      1. Each sprite shell has its own visible shell color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:22:#         cavity marker, not the shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:24:#      a blue shell containing an orange cavity marker slides flush to the separator.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:26:#      corresponding right-side rows, not blue. A green shell with a red marker emits red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:30:#    - Shell colors come from a small fixed shell palette, marker/ray colors from a second\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:31:#      small palette. The palettes are disjoint, so \"shell color\" and \"ray color\" are visibly\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:35:#    - More than two emitters naturally create repeated ray colors across different shell colors,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:36:#      which helps show that ray color does not come from shell identity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:38:#    - Original `left == black` sprite detection fails because shells are now multi-colored\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:40:#    - Original pixelwise shifting fails because cavity markers must move with the shell even\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:41:#      though they are not shell-colored pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:46:#      detect shell components from the shell-color mask, shift each shell's full bounding-box\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:47:#      patch, then detect enclosed non-shell regions and read the unique marker color from each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:51:#    - Shell colors are unique within each sample, so shell components never merge by color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:56:#      shell color, cavity marker color, and right-side ray color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:57:#    - Because shell and ray palettes are disjoint, samples directly show that matching the shell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:68:#    - Every shell is a single monochrome 4-connected component whose bbox contains all of its\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:148:def _shell_mask(left: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:154:    assert len(colors) == 1, f\"shell component must be monochrome, got {sorted(colors)}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:162:    comps = _components4(_shell_mask(left_src))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:163:    assert comps, \"expected at least one shell component\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:169:        assert delta >= 0, \"left-side shells must stay left of the separator\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:178:    for pts in _components4(~_shell_mask(left)):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:209:    Slide multi-colored shell sprites to the separator, then fire cavity-coded rays.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:213:    - Each left-side sprite has a monochrome shell color chosen independently from the other sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:214:    - Some enclosed holes inside those shells also contain a second, special marker color in addition to the background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:217:    - Move each sprite rightward until the shell's right edge is flush with the separator, carrying any hole markers along with it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:218:    - After sliding, find enclosed non-shell cavities; only cavities that touch the column just left of the separator emit.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:222:    - Shell color identifies which pixels belong to the same moving sprite, but ray color is not taken from that shell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:287:    shell_color: int,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:293:        patch[0, :mini_w] = shell_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:295:            patch[r, 0] = shell_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:296:            patch[r, mini_w - 1] = shell_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:297:        patch[mini_h - 1, :] = shell_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:298:        patch[-1, :] = shell_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:300:            patch[r, left_wall] = shell_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/16/code.py:301:            patch[r, right_wal