C_code/train/a2d730bd.py:262:            protrusions.update(cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/a2d730bd.py:266:            if protrusions & rect_cells or protrusions & marker_cells:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/a2d730bd.py:269:            reserved_cells = rect_cells | marker_cells | protrusions\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/a2d730bd.py:282:            for r, c in rect_cells | protrusions:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:3:# Name: 箭头形精灵凸出方向\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:15:# - This combo replaces the source object with arrow-shaped anchors and simultaneously changes the direction cue:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:16:#   the ray must follow the arrow's protruding head, not the side where the seed happens to touch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:18:#   Example: a right-facing arrow may have its seed above or below it, but the output still repeats that seed to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:24:# - Each grid uses at least two arrow orientations, so the shape cue is actually demonstrated inside one sample.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:26:# - `detect_dominant_big_component_color()` still works because arrows remain the only components with bbox >= 3x3.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:31:# - The generator is output-first: place full arrows and full rays first, then erase all but one long clue ray.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:32:# - Arrows, rays, and their 4-neighborhood guards are kept separate so two non-arrow components never merge under\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:33:#   `label_mask((grid != bg) & (grid != arrow_color))`.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:34:# - Candidate seeds are rejected if they go out of bounds, overlap, or even touch previously committed rays / arrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:36:# - The crucial cue is human-visible geometry: each arrow has one protruding tip and that tip points the repetition.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:38:# - The kept pre-extended clue ray shows that the repeated payload follows the arrow orientation rather than contact.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:41:# - No ray is allowed to touch a foreign arrow or another ray, so each object stays visually isolated.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:44:# - No ordering on color ids is used. Colors only separate background / arrow anchors / payload tiles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:47:# - For every generated arrow, the attachment side should be orthogonal to the true ray direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:50:# - Solver assumes each big anchor component exactly matches one rotated arrow template below.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:51:# - Solver assumes each arrow has exactly one adjacent non-arrow component (seed or pre-extended ray component).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:215:def _build_arrow_lookup() -> dict[tuple[tuple[int, ...], ...], tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:224:_ARROW_LOOKUP = _build_arrow_lookup()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:227:def _match_arrow_direction(mask: np.ndarray) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:254:def detect_arrow_component_color(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:260:    \"\"\"Choose the color whose big components best match the arrow template family.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:283:            if _match_arrow_direction(local) is not None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/cesh