y, bg: int) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D9/2/code.py:730:    src_pts = _colored_centroids(src, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D9/2/code.py:731:    dst_pts = _hole_centroids(dst, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/10/code.py:17:        arrow sample, so direction must be looked up from shape -> arrow, not hard-coded.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/10/code.py:65:   - The right side uses a fixed strip layout with one blank spacer column between shape and arrow,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/10/code.py:80:     3x3 shape patch at local cols 0..2 and a 3x3 arrow patch at local cols 4..6.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/10/code.py:123:# Right-side legend layout: one 3x3 shape sample + spacer + one 3x3 arrow sample.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/10/code.py:207:        arrow_patch = right[r0 : r0 + 3, LEGEND_ARROW_C0 : LEGEND_ARROW_C0 + 3]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/10/code.py:211:        glyph_to_dir[glyph_id] = _decode_dir_patch(arrow_patch, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/10/code.py:223:      glyph sample and a 3x3 arrow sample.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/10/code.py:450:        arrow_template = _DIR_TEMPLATES[glyph_to_dir[glyph_id]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/136b0064/10/code.py:455:            arrow_template * int(_LEGEND_ARROW_COLORS[glyph_to_dir[glyph_id]])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D2/0/code.py:83:    - Sort source blocks and dst holes by visible row-major order of bbox centers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D2/0/code.py:251:    This keeps bbox centers stable enough for visible row-major ordering.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/10/code.py:212:# For each shape color, connect its vertices in centroid-angle order, rotating the cycle\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/6/code.