troid-rank layout. Output is dst fully\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D3/0/code.py:40:#       src has 5 colored subsprites ordered by centroid rank:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6ffbe589/4/code.py:26:#     - match each cue to the board layer whose centroid is best aligned in row\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6ffbe589/4/code.py:31:#     - suppose the three input-layer centroids are near\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6ffbe589/4/code.py:55:#     centroids so that row/column alignment is not ambiguous.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6ffbe589/4/code.py:68:#   - The visible regularities are: which cue lines up with which centroid, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6ffbe589/4/code.py:260:    - Compute each board layer's centroid and match every outside cue to the layer with the closest row-or-column alignment.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/30/code.py:315:    Sort each color's pixels by angle around the centroid and consider consecutive\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D4/0/code.py:20:#    - dst contains empty holes in the same centroid-rank arrangement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D4/0/code.py:46:#      centroid-rank matching exactly as in the base task so D4 remains the only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D4/0/code.py:56:#      hole detection, centroid ranking, and transform search still operate on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/446ef5d2/11/code.py:66:#     To keep the task solvable, the generator narrows the rectangle size and piece\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D15/0/code.py:23:- The geometric rule is unchanged: match source subsprites to destination holes by centroid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D15/0/code.py:118:    match source colored subsprites to destination holes by centroid rank and fill them.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D3/0/code.py:32:#    - The old _angle_cycle() assumed the correct topology was a centroid-based cycle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/18/code.py:61:#    - To infer output orientation, the solver assumes object centroids span one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6ffbe589/6/code.py:74:#      to narrow strips on the middle box / inner box edges.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D18/2/code.py:11:    keep: src/dst extraction, centroid-rank matching, color transfer, tight crop\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D18/2/code.py:25:      - suppose dst has four matched holes ordered by centroid rank:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D18/2/code.py:40:    - transform search by centroid-rank still works because hole count and ordering are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D18/2/code.py:68:    - corresponding src/dst cavity centroids remain rank-matchable after rendering\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D18/2/code.py:290:    2. Match src colored subsprites to dst holes by centroid-rank pattern.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D3/3/code.py:124:def _centroid_hub(points_rc: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D3/3/code.py:172:        hub = _centroid_hub(pts_rc)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D3/3/code.py:215:# --------------- generator (star-centroid variant) ---------------\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/14/code.py:35:#    - \"holes can be found anywhere inside the bbox\" is narrowed to rectangular bg\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D3/2/code.py:15:#   old task: sort by polar angle around centroid, rotate the cycle so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D3/2/code.py:20:#   Vertices `[(0,0),(0,4),(3,4),(3,8)]` were formerly connected as a centroid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D6/2/code.py:28:#    - The matching rule stays the original centroid-rank pairing. This keeps inference focused\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D6/2/code.py:37:#    - Old solver only needed src colors, so it stored src component centroids/colors only.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D6/2/code.py:63:#    - The only color motion is the old, already-structured src->dst transfer by centroid rank.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/12/code.py:127:    Key insight: The puzzle is solved by a genuine two-step cue hierarchy: size only says which pieces can fit, marker count narrows the candidate slot set, and the marker layout inside equally counted rectangles determines the final correspondence.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/3/code.py:43:# - The destination structure changes visibly: wide bottom bars become narrow side bars.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D10/0/code.py:13:#   Original: pick the only src, rank-match all colored cavity centroids to all dst holes,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D10/0/code.py:27:#   Transform search used only src colored centroids; invalid for partial srcs because a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/8/code.py:19:#      line carries a same-colored protrusion mask;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/8/code.py:21:#      on each active side must equal the frame protrusion mask on that side;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/8/code.py:30:#      mask equals the top protrusion comb and whose left-hole mask equals the left protrusion comb.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/8/code.py:32:#    - integration detail: because D1 uses the second row/column for protrusions, the D5 copy target\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/8/code.py:49:#    - Naively reusing the D5 corner target `(1,1)` would overwrite D1 protrusions on row/col 1; the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/8/code.py:57:#    - The frame protrusion masks are kept away from the literal corner, so the two control colors never\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/8/code.py:58:#      overwrite each other and the copied core does not overlap the protrusion lane.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/8/code.py:63:#    - The protrusion lane remains visible in the output because the corner copy is offset inward; this\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/8/code.py:315:    2. Read the inner protrusion masks on those two sides.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/8/code.py:316:    3. Find the unique dihedral transform whose object-side hole masks equal those protrusion masks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D11/0/code.py:215:    - The true dst is the unique empty frame whose hole centroid-rank signature matches\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/49/code.py:26:#     The family is intentionally narrow: one basin template, one erasable source component, one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/1/code.py:15:#    border colors, but the inner line next to each active frame side also carries a protrusion\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/1/code.py:17:#    guide masks exactly match those frame protrusion masks, then peel off the guide cells seen\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/1/code.py:22:#    positions as the top frame protrusions, and likewise for the left frontier. Near the notch,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/1/code.py:44:#    protrusions are painted on the inner border line and the object is placed with `border=1`,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/1/code.py:49:#    directions, and the frame carries matching comb-like protrusions on one horizontal plus one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/1/code.py:54:#    the border/protrusions only. Internal pattern colors stay inside the core. This avoids heavy\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/1/code.py:247:    Align a non-rectangular object by matching guide-hole signatures to frame protrusions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/1/code.py:251:    the one whose directional frontier guide mask matches the two frame protrusion masks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/18/code.py:35:#    - The basin family is deliberately narrow: two adjacent cups with an optional overflow divider.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/2/code.py:59:    - B pieces are narrow rectangles placed far enough from the notch columns to avoid overlap inside bars\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/43/code.py:16:#      The generated landform is a high right-side shelf beside a narrow vertical chute; a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D1/3/code.py:37:     once widths vary, placing a wide shape into a narrow slot can overlap neighbors unless\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D14/0/code.py:126:    assert w >= 2, \"grid too narrow for legend\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D1/7/code.py:61:#    orders them from narrowest baseline contact to widest. Because colors stay tied to slots\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/25/code.py:37:#    The family is deliberately narrow:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/26/code.py:431:def _add_right_source(g: np.ndarray, top_row: int, narrow_rows: int, color: int) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/26/code.py:474:        narrow_rows = 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/26/code.py:482:        _add_right_source(g, right_top, narrow_rows, right_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:29:#        (r0 + dr*h, c0 + dc*w) became the template centroid position, so the copy\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:30:#        top-left had to be shifted by the template centroid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:37:#        3. compute that rotated version's own pixel centroid;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:38:#        4. treat (r0 + dr*size, c0 + dc*size) as that centroid's target location;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:41:#        suppose the canonical local centroid is (1.75, 1.00).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:42:#        The 90-degree version then has centroid (1.00, 1.25).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:53:#      bbox, be rotationally asymmetric, and have quadrant-dependent centroid shifts\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:64:#      positions for the rotated centroid, so an additional centroid-dependent\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:77:#    - Generator enumerates template origins only where every rotated-centroid stamp\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:87:#      2. copies are not aligned by bbox top-left, but by the rotated shape centroid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:92:#      silhouette remains legible and the centroid shifts are not hidden by large\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:98:#      centroid-only, or rotation-only output, ensuring both control dimensions\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:125:def _template_centroid(cells: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> tuple[float, float]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:156:        centroid_r, centroid_c = _template_centroid(rot_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:157:        cache[turns] = (rot_cells, centroid_r, centroid_c)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:167:    centroid_r: float,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:168:    centroid_c: float,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:170:    use_centroid: bool,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:174:    if not use_centroid:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:176:    return _round_nearest(anchor_r - centroid_r), _round_nearest(anchor_c - centroid_c)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:191:    use_centroid: bool,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:199:        rot_cells, centroid_r, centroid_c = rotations[turns]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:206:            centroid_r,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:207:            centroid_c,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:208:            use_centroid=use_centroid,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:233:    use_centroid: bool,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:239:        rot_cells, centroid_r, centroid_c = rotations[turns]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:246:            centroid_r,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:247:            centroid_c,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:248:            use_centroid=use_centroid,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:263:    use_centroid: bool,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:313:        rot_cells, centroid_r, centroid_c = rotations[turns]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:320:            centroid_r,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:321:            centroid_c,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:322:            use_centroid=use_centroid,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:342:    Stamp quadrant-rotated copies of a monochrome template, but align each copy by the rotated template centroid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:352:    - Turn `(r0 + dr*size, c0 + dc*size)` into the target location of that rotated stamp's pixel centroid, then round back to an integer top-left and place the whole rotated copy there.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:356:    - The singleton lattice controls both which copies appear and how they are oriented, but the placement anchor is no longer the bbox corner; it is the centroid of the quadrant-selected rotated shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:358:    return _solver_output(grid, use_centroid=True, use_quadrant_rotation=True)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:430:def _has_quadrant_dependent_centroid_shift(cells: list[tuple[int, int]], size: int) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:434:        centroid_r, centroid_c = _template_centroid(rot_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:435:        offsets.add((_round_nearest(-centroid_r), _round_nearest(-centroid_c)))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:448:        if not _has_quadrant_dependent_centroid_shift(cells, size):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:481:            _rot_cells, centroid_r, _centroid_c = rotations[turns]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:482:            shift_r = _round_nearest(r0 + dr * size - centroid_r)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:493:            _rot_cells, _centroid_r, centroid_c = rotations[turns]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:494:            shift_c = _round_nearest(c0 + dc * size - centroid_c)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:506:    centroid_only = _solver_output(grid, use_centroid=True, use_quadrant_rotation=False)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:507:    rotation_only = _solver_output(grid, use_centroid=False, use_quadrant_rotation=True)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:508:    original = _solver_output(grid, use_centroid=False, use_quadrant_rotation=False)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:509:    diff_vs_centroid = int(np.count_nonzero(combo != centroid_only))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:512:    return diff_vs_centroid, diff_vs_rotation, diff_vs_original\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:569:        diff_vs_centroid, diff_vs_rotation, diff_vs_original = _variant_diffs(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:570:        if diff_vs_centroid < 4:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:606:            use_centroid=True,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/20/code.py:623:            use_centroid=True,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/27/code.py:25:# - The geometry is deliberately narrow: always two adjacent basins, always a shorter\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D4/2/code.py:20:   - To make tight-crop observable, the generator narrows the baseline from “full row”\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/13/code.py:28:#    accent's proportional horizontal centroid, while the visible hole reinforces\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/13/code.py:184:      accent's horizontal centroid rather than from the sprite's original x; keep the hole transparent.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/40/code.py:10:#    active frame side owns a same-colored inward protrusion mask on the adjacent inner line. The object also has\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/40/code.py:13:#    protrusion masks on the same sides, then crop the matched guide layer, then apply one extra reflection to the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/40/code.py:35:#    `paste`. The frame protrusions live on the inner border line of the active sides only; the object is placed with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/40/code.py:36:#    `border=1`, so it cannot overlap the frame controls or their protrusions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/40/code.py:40:#    border protrusions after axis alignment, and (4) the output is the cropped rectangle but reflected along the axis\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/40/code.py:43:#    The two frame protrusion masks on opposite sides share one projected span, which keeps the scene tidy rather than\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/40/code.py:54:#    - `_frame_signature()` assumes each active side has exactly one contiguous span of protrusion positions with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/8/code.py:17:#    - The fused change fixes the lower area to a long chain of 4 or 5 narrow basins. The top\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/8/code.py:288:    - Bottom-anchored solids form a chain of 4 or 5 narrow basins separated by single divider walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/24/code.py:37:#    - or, for the narrower layout, the same receiver with one inner step.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/33/code.py:33:#    The geometry is intentionally narrow and repetitive rather than highly free-form:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:35:#   centroid of the filled template pixels. The rendered bbox top-left is therefore\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:36:#   round((r0 + dr*h, c0 + dc*w) - centroid(mask)), so the output array usually shifts\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:38:# - Example: if a 4x3 template has filled centroid (1.5, 1.0), then the origin copy\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:40:#   Ordinary copies keep the positive holey mask at similarly centroid-aligned sites,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:50:# - The generator also rejects samples where centroid anchoring is too close to plain\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:64:# - Hole handling matters in two places: centroid computation must ignore holes because\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:70:# - Every centroid-aligned bbox is kept fully inside the 22x22 grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:79:# - Because the negative copy is also centroid-shifted, its bbox typically no longer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:114:def _template_centroid(templ_rel: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> tuple[float, float]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:127:    centroid_r: float,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:128:    centroid_c: float,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:136:    if anchor_mode == \"centroid\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:137:        return _round_nearest(anchor_r - centroid_r), _round_nearest(anchor_c - centroid_c)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:214:    centroid_r, centroid_c = _template_centroid(templ_rel)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:236:            r0, c0, dr, dc, h, w, centroid_r, centroid_c, anchor_mode=anchor_mode\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:274:    Replicate a holey template from a singleton lattice, but place every copy by centroid alignment and render the origin as a complement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:283:    - Use each offset to move a centroid anchor by (dr*h, dc*w), where h and w are the template bbox dimensions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:284:    - Convert that anchor back to a bbox top-left by subtracting the template centroid and rounding to grid cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:288:    - The copied object is not just \"the bbox\" and not just \"the positive sprite\": holes change the centroid used for placement, while the distinguished origin copy flips filled-vs-empty inside the same bbox.\n/home/lixinyu/sna