:#    - Reachable vs stuck examples differ by a visible local narrowing on a later ring or turn. The side bulge\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D5/2/code.py:237:    Recolor each piece by quantizing its centroid into a k×k grid, using legend_map.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D5/2/code.py:363:    - Recolor each assembled piece by the legend color corresponding to the piece centroid's quadrant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:18:#    - In this combo, each active source endpoint becomes a 3-cell blue L-arrow. The degree-2\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:19:#      corner is the tip; the missing quadrant is the arrow's forward diagonal direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:20:#    - Each arrow also has exactly one orthogonally adjacent marker cell in a non-blue,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:21:#      non-magenta color. Marker colors are the pairing labels: two arrows with the same marker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:22:#      color form one active pair. The segment is drawn between their tips, and both arrows must\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:24:#    - Example: suppose arrows A and B have red markers. A's tip is at (3,3) and points SE;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:26:#      inside the arrow bodies and could not tell which blue cells are endpoints. New logic first\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:27:#      parses each 4-connected 3-cell L, extracts its tip/direction, groups arrows by marker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:31:#      arrow distractor on the same diagonal extension as a real pair. Geometry-only pairing would\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:40:#    - At most one uniquely marked distractor arrow is added. That is enough to make marker-based\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:44:#    - The old `by_color[line_color]` pool is invalid because a single arrow contains three blue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:51:#      3-cell L arrow, each such arrow must have exactly one adjacent marker, active marker colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:52:#      must appear on exactly two arrows, and those two arrows must face each other along a shared\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:59:#      distractor arrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:60:#    - Marker cells are attached to the tip side of an arrow, stay off all active diagonals and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:61:#      future rays, and touch only their own arrow in 4-neighborhood.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:63:#      arrow unambiguously.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:66:#    - Humans can directly see the L-arrow cue and infer that the diagonal leaves the tip through\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:68:#    - Repeated marker colors across distant arrows make the pairing label visible in a few\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:71:#      then connect arrow tips\" is more plausible than any accidental one-off geometry heuristic.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:76:#    - Markers sit beside arrow tips instead of on the diagonal itself, so arrows, labels, path\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:78:#    - Distractor arrows, when present, are placed on diagonal extensions outside the active\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:82:#    - Marker colors do not transform into output colors; they only label which arrows belong\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:123:def _arrow_cells(tip: tuple[int, 