D5/2/code.py:90:#     much shorter/narrower than the original single-column lattice\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/24/code.py:41:#   \"which frame fits which protrusion\" relation visually learnable across a few examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:7:#    - Keep the original visible vocabulary: monochrome 3-cell L-arrows, sparse mono-color wall\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:9:#    - Fused change 1 (D8/0): arrows are no longer processed in arbitrary detection order. They\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:10:#      fire from near-center to far-center, where \"center distance\" is measured from the arrow's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:15:#    - Small example: suppose arrow A starts nearer the center and paints\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:20:#    - The generator uses only 2-3 arrows. This is enough to make sequential dependence visible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:22:#    - The first arrow is biased toward the center and is long, usually with 1-2 static-wall\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:24:#    - Later arrows are biased to be farther from the center and to terminate on prior track,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:27:#    - Original assumption: arrow iteration order is irrelevant. Broken by the combo; solver now\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:29:#    - Original assumption: only static non-arrow pixels matter as blockers. Broken by the combo;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:37:#    - Generator keeps all input arrows and static walls pairwise disjoint and in-bounds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:38:#    - It also reserves every planned output ray cell in a global occupied set, so no later arrow,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:43:#    - The order cue is human-visible geometry, not hidden color ranking: nearer-to-center arrows\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:60:#    - Solver assumes arrow starts are valid L-corners and can be totally ordered by center\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:77:def _is_arrow_pts(pts: list[Coord]) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:85:def _arrow_dir_and_start(pts: list[Coord]) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], Coord] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:109:def _arrow_points_from_start(start: Coord, direction: tuple[int, int]) -> list[Coord]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:129:def _detect_arrows(g: np.ndarray, bg: int) -> tuple[list[dict[str, object]], set[Coord]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:131:    arrows: list[dict[str, object]] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:132:    arrow_cells: set[Coord] = set()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:136:            if not _is_arrow_pts(pts):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:138:            info = _arrow_dir_and_start(pts)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:142:            arrows.append(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:151:            arrow_cells |= set(pts)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:152:    arrows.sort(key=lambda a: a[\"order_key\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:153:    return arrows, arrow_cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:156:def _trace_arrow(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:159:    arrow: dict[str, object],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/13/code.py:161:    arrow_cells: set[Coord],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca36