/a47bf94d/D1/3/code.py:593:    at those cells the tracer can keep going straight unless it reads the local arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/4/code.py:64:# Marker templates are centered on the landing cell. The arrow direction becomes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/4/code.py:83:#   arrow glyphs. The center of each glyph is still the landing cell, but the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/4/code.py:88:#   2. The consumed marker at H1 carries an arrow, say \"Down\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/4/code.py:91:#   4. Therefore the same visible arrow on the marker is both a turn command\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/4/code.py:98:# - Only one extra object family is introduced: a compact 5-cell arrow glyph in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/4/code.py:134:#   while the consumed marker's own arrow tells \"how to face next\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/4/code.py:143:#   merges with the arrow glyphs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/4/code.py:147:#   arrows, the last snapshot remains readable even with multi-step lookahead.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/4/code.py:338:    - Each frame contains one actor-colored triangle plus marker-colored mini-arrow glyphs whose center cells are future landing points.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/4/code.py:343:    - When a marker is consumed, the marker's own arrow sets the new facing; if markers remain, that arrow direction must also be the direction of the next marker that will be consumed from the new head.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/4/code.py:346:    Key insight: The triangle tip tells you which marker is eaten now, while the eaten marker's arrow tells you how the sprite must face for the next leg, so every step couples local consumption with one-step lookahead.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/23/code.py:1