“中心对齐”前提；融合后该前提失效，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/271d71e2/6/code.py:26:#     The final box is two cells narrower and the surviving interior contains two bg holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/221dfab4/D10/1/code.py:29:#    stripe's current narrowed span. Green stripes still recolor the entire row/column's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/221dfab4/D10/1/code.py:30:#    existing non-background pixels to green before repainting the narrowed stripe cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/221dfab4/D10/1/code.py:49:#    and at least one green flood changes a foreground pixel outside the narrowed stripe.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:77:                \"narrow\": {\"segment\": [(-2, 0)], \"flanks\": [(-2, -1), (-2, 1)], \"width\": 1},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:85:                \"narrow\": {\"segment\": [(-4, 0)], \"flanks\": [(-4, -1), (-4, 1)], \"width\": 1},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:97:                \"narrow\": {\"segment\": [(0, 2)], \"flanks\": [(-1, 2), (1, 2)], \"width\": 1},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:105:                \"narrow\": {\"segment\": [(0, 4)], \"flanks\": [(-1, 4), (1, 4)], \"width\": 1},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:117:                \"narrow\": {\"segment\": [(2, 0)], \"flanks\": [(2, -1), (2, 1)], \"width\": 1},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:125:                \"narrow\": {\"segment\": [(4, 0)], \"flanks\": [(4, -1), (4, 1)], \"width\": 1},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:137:                \"narrow\": {\"segment\": [(0, -2)], \"flanks\": [(-1, -2), (1, -2)], \"width\": 1},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/39/code.py:145:                \"narrow\": {\"segment\": [(0, -4)], \"flanks\": [(-1, -4), (1, -4)], \"width\": 1},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D14/1/code.py:70:      sign(centroid(indicator) - centroid(center))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D14/1/code.py:198:    Slide yellow pixels inside walled regions in the direction dictated by border-legend arrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D13/2/code.py:45:#    only directional cue is the external 2-pixel arrow-like marker. Across samples, the same closed wall\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D20/1/code.py:111:      sign(centroid(indicator) - centroid(center))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D2/0/code.py:22:#       into the narrow side column. In this variant, adjacent corner-style exits are dead:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D2/0/code.py:49:#     - Therefore the variant redefines horizontal reachability narrowly: the drop column must\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D2/0/code.py:95:    shafts plus longer flat shelves, so narrow step chutes no longer connect basins.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/6/code.py:528:    # Distance to bbox is more visually stable than centroid distance for selecting the target wall.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D21/1/code.py:119:      sign(centroid(indicator) - centroid(center))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D6/2/code.py:69:    Fill a bottle-shaped enclosure, forcing the color through a narrow neck before it fans outward.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:207:    Move a compact water plug through a wall-bounded corridor until the corridor ends or narrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:212:    - The source plug starts at one endpoint of the reachable corridor. Downstream sections may bend and may later narrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:218:    - Relocate the plug to the last reachable placement before the corridor terminates or becomes too narrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D7/2/code.py:76:    The sign of centroid(indicator) - centroid(center) defines the direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/2/code.py:16:#    \"air\" is no longer the transport medium. Instead, color 8 marks a narrow pipe network.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D22/2/code.py:12:      - center->indicator centroid offset still encodes the slide direction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D22/2/code.py:87:    The other two colors are the center color and the indicator color. Their centroid offset\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D22/2/code.py:135:        center_centroid = np.mean(np.array(center, dtype=float), axis=0)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D22/2/code.py:136:        indicator_centroid = np.mean(np.array(indicator, dtype=float), axis=0)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D22/2/code.py:137:        vr, vc = (indicator_centroid - center_centroid).tolist()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D22/2/code.py:183:    Slide red pixels inside walled regions in the direction dictated by border-legend arrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/29/code.py:11:#       1. clean one-cell foreground noise and boundary protrusions\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/29/code.py:40:#   - `_clean_foreground` still assumes all corruption is one-cell noise/protrusions; the generator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/29/code.py:107:    Remove one-cell specks/protrusions before detecting black dents.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D3/1/code.py:240:    - The remaining colors form fixed shelves, walls, and narrow reservoirs anchored to the lower half.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/bf45cf4b/15/code.py:55:# - The rule space is intentionally narrow: exactly one component, one mask, and exactly 2 rounds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/18/code.py:20:#    (horizontal or vertical through the region bbox center). Dent centers are repaired\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/18/code.py:78:    Remove one-cell specks/protrusions before detecting black dents.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/18/code.py:345:      back to black and one-cell cross-color protrusions are restored to their host.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/34/code.py:203:    - Magenta walls carve the board into a narrow maze.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D4/1/code.py:231:    narrow_rows = rng.randint(0, min(2, 9 - source_top))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D4/1/code.py:236:        cols = [9] if r < source_top + narrow_rows else [8, 9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/25/code.py:160:      one-cell boundary protrusions revert to the surrounding region color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:9:#     - The D11 change is a single-color thin arrow placed in the open corridor between those two\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:10:#       training frames. The arrow is horizontal or vertical and points from source frame to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:19:#         - solver locates the arrow component in the gap between those two frames\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:20:#         - arrow tip decides which frame is destination, so only one direction is inferred\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:22:#       - horizontal arrow = 1-pixel shaft plus a 3-pixel head inside the frame gap\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:23:#       - vertical arrow = same idea rotated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:28:#       adjacent, which makes the arrow legible and avoids diagonal-direction ambiguity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:32:#     - find_square_frames(): still valid because the arrow never touches a frame border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D11/0/code.py:33:#     - blank-frame detection: unchanged; the