   Remove one-cell specks/protrusions before detecting black dents.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D1/3/code.py:178:      or protrusions near the region boundaries.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D3/3/code.py:38:in a narrow, human-countable range (3-5 pixels per source). This avoids noisy\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D3/3/code.py:271:        raise RuntimeError(\"source side too narrow for sparse component\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/36/code.py:107:    Remove one-cell specks and protrusions before reading dent geometry.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/36/code.py:214:      isolated specks fall back to black, and one-cell protrusions revert to the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D1/2/code.py:101:    Remove one-cell specks/protrusions before detecting black dents.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D1/2/code.py:213:      one-cell color specks or boundary protrusions that should be cleaned away.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D1/2/code.py:219:      isolated specks revert to black, and one-cell cross-color protrusions are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/28/code.py:65:#    - Grey sprites remain single connected objects, and their protrusions are added only from the exterior,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/28/code.py:542:def _add_protrusions(mask: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/28/code.py:567:        mask = _add_protrusions(mask)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D9/2/code.py:14:# - The objects stay the same: one arrow-like triangle plus single-pixel markers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D9/2/code.py:312:    Continue an arrow sprite from the latest usable reversed snapshot until all markers vanish.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/20/code.py:47:#     agree with the row band of the placement centroid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8