/1/code.py:97:    Remove one-cell specks/protrusions before detecting black dents.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D12/1/code.py:240:      one-cell cross-color protrusions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/23/code.py:12:#    next cleanup it is shaved into small black gaps/protrusions, and those new black cells can\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/23/code.py:303:    - Work in rounds. In each round, first clean the current foreground arrangement until local one-cell noise/protrusions are stable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/25/code.py:12:  sprites are forced into a very narrow outer ring).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/25/code.py:37:- The sprite band is intentionally narrow, but not so narrow that generation becomes impossible. A fixed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/25/code.py:41:  That gives enough variety for matching while avoiding impossible 3x3-like sprites in the narrow ring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/25/code.py:51:  assumption, so sprite generation must use a narrower shape library and lower sprite counts.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/25/code.py:92:  2. The outside sprite region is only the narrow perimeter ring around that large frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/25/code.py:282:# Sprite scattering in the narrow edge ring\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/25/code.py:464:    \"\"\"Try to place one sprite in the narrow edge ring.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/1ae2feb7/D4/2/code.py:217:        raise ValueError(\"bar side too narrow for sampled separator gap\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/6/code.py:55:#    - Each indentation is a single narrow rectangular notch. No extra markers are added.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/22/code.py:113:    Remove one-cell specks/protrusions before detecting black dents.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D4/0/code.py:47:#     centroid-based role inference is stable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D4/0/code.py:119:    Remove one-cell specks/protrusions before detecting black dents.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:18:#    The visible sprites are now 3-pixel arrows in 8 compass facings, so the input suggests\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:19:#    \"follow the arrow tip\". The fusion rule breaks that expectation: the tip still marks the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:22:#      cells {(3,6),(4,5),(4,6)} form a NE-looking arrow with tip (3,6).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:28:#      fires upward to an in-bounds cell even though the arrow still visually points NE.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:33:#    - Keep exactly 8 arrow templates and exactly 4 actual firing directions (toward top/bottom/\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:35:#    - Require both diagonal-looking and axis-looking arrows in each generated grid; otherwise the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:37:#    - Require repeated evidence that arrows are misleading: several sprites must fire in a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:43:#      combo, only emitter recovery survives, and it must be replaced by arrow-template matching.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:51:#    - Generation precomputes all arrow placements whose 3 cells are in bounds, whose nearest edge\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:55:#    - Under this toward-edge geometry, legal 5-step destinations stay in narrow border bands.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:61:#    - The crucial observable is disagreement between arrow facing and actual shot direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:63:#      arrow\" solver on the same input.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:65:#      arrow facings within at least one shared nearest-edge class.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:78:#    - For each sprite, compare `visual_dir` from the arrow template with `actual_dir` from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:84:#    - Every non-bg component is exactly one 3-pixel arrow matching a unique template.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:85:#    - Every generated arrow has a unique nearest edge; ties are excluded.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:86:#    - The projectile always starts from the arrow tip, not from any other pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:138:def _arrow_tip_and_dir(comp: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int]] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:175:def _arrow_tip_and_edge_dir(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:180:    tip_data = _arrow_tip_and_dir(comp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:193:    Fire projectiles from 3-pixel arrow sprites, but aim them by border proximity instead of arrow facing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:197:    - Every non-background 8-connected component is a monochrome 3-pixel arrow in one of 8 visual facings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:198:    - The arrow tip still identifies the launch cell, but the arrow's pointing direction is not the movement rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:201:    - Match each component to an arrow template to recover its tip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:206:    Key insight: The arrowhead is a red herring. Shape tells you where the shot starts, but the shot direction comes from the sprite's global position relative to the border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:223:        td = _arrow_tip_and_edge_dir(comp, h, w)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:267:        td = _arrow_tip_and_dir(comp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/10/code.py:429:        if _arrow_tip_and_edge_dir(coords, H, W) is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/41/code.py:110:    Remove one-cell specks/protrusions before detecting black dents.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/41/code.py:226:      or short protrusions near the boundary between the two regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D13/0/code.py:192:    Remove one-cell specks/protrusions before detecting black dents.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D13/0/code.py:282:    - The large regions still contain black dents plus a few one-cell color specks or protrusions near boundaries.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D13/0/code.py:286:    - Locally clean the two large regions: isolated specks become black, and one-cell cross-color protrusions revert to the surrounding region color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D8/0/code.py:269:    - Each frame contains one triangular arrow sprite plus isolated one-pixel markers, all in the same actor color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D13/1/code.py:106:    Remove one-cell specks/protrusions before detecting black dents.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D13/1/code.py:183:      or protrusions along region boundaries.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/6/code.py:90:    Remove one-cell specks/protrusions before detecting black dents.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D8/3/code.py:33:#       - Original: final simulated frame is an 11x13 canvas with a 3x3 arrow near row 7,col 9.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D8/3/code.py:34:#       - Old solver: returned the whole 11x13 canvas with only that arrow painted.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D8/3/code.py:36:#         to the arrow's occupied bbox, returning only a 3x3 patch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D8/3/code.py:40:#     - This is intentionally a narrow D8-only edit, matching the reference task\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D13/2/code.py:84:    Remove one-cell specks/protrusions before detecting black dents.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D13/2/code.py:153:      or boundary protrusions that should be cleaned first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D13/2/code.py:157:      original task: isolated specks become black and wrong-color protrusions\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/36/code.py:300:    - The puzzle is no longer solved in one placement pass: color first tells which scraps belong together, then color semantics narrow the vertical band, and finally the ordered row layout resolves which same-band chamber each assembled subcomponent occupies.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D1/0/code.py:8:#    The triangle sprite remains a monochrome arrow and the input still contains\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D1/0/code.py:14:#    still axis-aligned so the arrow orientation can keep tracking travel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D1/0/code.py:269:    Key insight: The arrow shape still gives the sprite's current head and facing, but target selection no longer depends on directional alignment; it depends on matching the sprite color to the left half of the remaining colored domino chain.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/14/code.py:204:    - The corruptions come in two kinds: cross-color boundary protrusions between the main regions, and isolated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/14/code.py:209:      regions: boundary protrusions are recolored into the locally dominant region, while isolated background specks\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D1/1/code.py:22:#   difference: the path is driven by global distance, not by the arrow tip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D1/1/code.py:59:#   continuation rather than to the arrow tip's current direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D1/1/code.py:277:    Key insight: The arrow tip still tells you how the sprite is drawn after each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D18/0/code.py:75:    Remove one-cell specks/protrusions before detecting black dents.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D6/1/code.py:3:# Change: 变换前先清洁前景区域：移除背景/边缘区域中的孤立前景色斑点（single-cell specks），将单像素边界突出（protrusion）重着色为周围区域色\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D6/1/code.py:11:#    - Cross-color boundary protrusions still behave like before: they are recolored into the surrounding region, not marked teal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D6/1/code.py:169:      foreground specks in background/outer-edge areas, others are cross-color boundary protrusions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D6/1/code.py:173:      removable isolated specks are treated as background, while boundary protrusions are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:18:#         protrusions back into the surrounding host region;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:25:#      3) each one-cell region-region protrusion is no longer erased semantically:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:34:#      old protrusion:   [a a a]      old cleanup/output center -> a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:37:#      combo protrusion: cleanup still says host is `a`, but the final output center\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:38:#      is teal at that same location, so protrusions remain visible instead of vanishing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:41:#    - The combo would collapse visually if samples had only dents or only protrusions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:42:#      The generator therefore enforces both: many dents and 3-6 protrusions per sample.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:51:#    - The original `_clean_foreground` treated protrusions as disposable corruption.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:53:#      baseline reconstruction step before we re-mark protrusion cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:55:#      both combo signals: dent centers would not be forced back to black, and protrusion\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:58:#      because protrusions are handled by a separate detector on foreground cells whose\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:62:#    - Dents and protrusions use global Chebyshev separation >= 3, except for optional\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:64:#      and prevents protrusion markers from landing inside a dent patch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:68:#      removable noise rather than creating accidental new protrusions or dents.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:79:#      protrusion markers. That is still a compact palette.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:80:#    - Because protrusions are not expanded into patches in this combo, teal remains a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:90:#      non-black one-cell protrusion -> teal point.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:91:#    - Repeated examples support the inference that teal means \"protrusion\" while black\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:95:#    - Every protrusion marker in the output must correspond to an input foreground cell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:100:#    - No protrusion center may fall inside any dent patch, or the teal marker would\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:117:# --- CFG: protrusions ---\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:161:    protrusions collapse back into the local host region. The combo then reuses this\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:163:    were protrusions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:215:def _protrusion_centers(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:247:    Turn black dents into hollow opposite-color patches and keep protrusions as teal markers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:252:      and a few one-cell protrusions where one foreground color pokes into the other.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:256:      specks and collapsing one-cell protrusions back into the surrounding host region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:260:    - Every original one-cell protrusion that cleanup rewrites into the other foreground\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:267:      that cleanup erases as protrusions are reintroduced as teal markers. Teal therefore\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:268:      marks protrusions only, and black can mean either true background or a dent center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:277:    protrusions = _protrusion_centers(g, clean, colors)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:287:    for r, c in protrusions:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:424:def _neighbor_protrusion_safe(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:455:def _safe_protrusion_candidate(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:489:    if not _neighbor_protrusion_safe(clean, r, c, source, host, bg):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/12/code.py:494:def _find_protrusion_candidates(\