/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/16/code.py:26:#          carve long narrow chambers rather than roughly square rooms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/11/code.py:270:    Draw red outer outlines, but count both true holes and deep narrow indentations when choosing the recolor tier.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:36:#      component, orthogonal rooms, and a small number of narrow chokepoints.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/9/code.py:48:#      narrow doorway would be mistaken for a real passage and the maze would\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D4/0/code.py:11:# - The changed behavior is narrow but important: the next marker is now chosen as\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/37/code.py:29:#      skipped (<= 10), narrow-halo (11-15), and wide-halo (>= 16).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:289:    Recolor particles as they thread through a narrow corridor, using alternating turn priority with a backup turn.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:298:    - Because the path is a narrow corridor, the particle keeps moving straight until the corridor wall blocks its next cell; that blocked wall cell is marked with the end color if it is background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:323:    \"\"\"Reject local rooms so the path reads as a narrow 1-2 cell corridor.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:348:    \"\"\"Build a single narrow serpentine corridor that guarantees an early fallback turn.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:388:    # At most one gentle width-2 bulge keeps the corridor visibly narrow instead of turning it into a room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D4/1/code.py:286:    - Each frame contains one triangular arrow sprite plus same-color single-pixel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D4/1/code.py:299:    Key insight