 Recolor that hollow component to teal when its centroid is in the left half of the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D8/1/code.py:126:      grid, or to green when its centroid is in the right half, then draw the outline.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D8/1/code.py:376:def _local_centroid_col(mask: np.ndarray) -> float:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D8/1/code.py:383:    centroid_col = _local_centroid_col(mask) + float(c)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D8/1/code.py:386:        return centroid_col <= midpoint - HOLLOW_SIDE_MARGIN\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D8/1/code.py:387:    return centroid_col >= midpoint + HOLLOW_SIDE_MARGIN\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9aaea919/D1/4/code.py:37:#    人类能直接看到：哪几条车道的底部接出“尾巴”，哪条车道下方有“箭头头部”，因此能推断转移方向是 tail -> arrowhead。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9aaea919/D1/4/code.py:135:                assert target is None, \"expected a single target arrowhead\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9aaea919/D1/4/code.py:154:    - A third-color connector sits in the bottom two rows: source lanes show thin tails; the destination lane shows a 3-pixel arrowhead.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9aaea919/D1/4/code.py:158:    - The arrow-headed destination lane receives the same number of new sprites, stacked upward into empty lattice slots and recolored to that lane's color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a32d8b75/D16/1/code.py:456:MIN_CANVAS_W = 8                # reject if canvas narrower than this\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D2/1/code.py:290:    alignment key. Shape and symmetry narrow the options, and the anchor markers finish the match.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/247ef758/D12/0/code.py:22:# - 原 `main()` 中 `cr/cc = bbox center` 与 `dr/dc = target - center` 明确依赖“中心对齐”前提；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a32d8b75/D3/0/code.py:52:#   - The legend panel stays narrow and orderly: sprite at top, outer frame, inner frame,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58490d8a/16/code.py:43:#      bbox center as its tally anchor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9aaea919/D4/0/code.py:54:#    single narrow example family.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a32d8b75/D12/0/code.py:31:#    The change is intentionally narrow. Object parsing, color-swap, frame\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/64efde09/D14/2/code.py:181:    - Several dense 2-by-N or N-by-2 rectangular sprites are dihedral transforms of one narrow template.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/247ef758/D4/2/code.py:118:      sprites in a narrow left strip separated by a constant-color divider column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a32d8b75/D7/2/code.py:254:    - The bottom symbol is no longer a directional arrow. It is a count code, so a solver must ignore the hand's orientation and decode only how many color-7 pixels extend away from the center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D10/2/code.py:225:    Add red outlines around objects, and also treat deep narrow indentations as holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D10/2/code.py:229:    - Some objects have true enclosed holes; others may instead have a narrow deep notch that opens to the outside from one side of the object's tight bounding box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D10/2/code.py:233:    - If a component has either enclosed holes or deep narrow boundary indentations, recolor the component to teal (8).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/13/code.py:98:#      detached components. This gives the learner repeated evidence that color narrows the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D11/1/code.py:49:#    Cluster-local columns are narrow and outlines stay disjoint, so there is no dense overlap of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D15/2/code.py:30:#       sort outline cells by clockwise polar angle around the component bbox center, then\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:21:#     variant: a 3-pixel green arrowhead/V marker:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:29:#       - the arrowhead orientation, not border contact alone, determines the main travel direction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:37:#       - inside that component, the unique degree-2 cell is the arrow tip\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:65:#   - humans can read the marker as an arrowhead/V immediately; there is no hidden color-id convention\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:71:#   - that component forms a valid arrowhead with one degree-2 tip and two symmetric wing cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:76:    \"\"\"Return (start_row, start_col, init_dir) from a 3-pixel arrowhead marker.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:93:    assert len(tips) == 1 and len(wings) == 2, \"green marker must be an arrowhead\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:109:    - The path source is a 3-pixel green arrowhead near one border, not a single pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:110:    - The arrowhead's orientation encodes the path's initial direction; its interior tip is the actual start cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:113:    - Decode the arrowhead direction from its shape, then aim for the opposite grid edge along that axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D5/2/code.py:129:    # --- decode the unique green arrowhead marker ---\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/22/code.py:28:#     to the geometric centroid (the true centroid falls between cells because the rectangles are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/22/code.py:31:#     that centroid-adjacent hub along three cardinal directions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/22/code.py:39:#       below a central hub just inside the rectangle near the sprite centroid. Output rays also\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/22/code.py:47:#   - Restricting control ports to exactly three structural positions prevents centroid-launched\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/22/code.py:55:#     active-edge cell. This is false now because the launch origin moved to a centroid-adjacent\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/22/code.py:286:    Read internal marker colors as labels for three structural ports of a shared sprite template, then emit those colors from each sprite's centroid-adjacent hub.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/22/code.py:291:    - Three isolated single-pixel markers sit strictly inside the canvas on clear cardinal rays extending away from a sprite's centroid-side hub.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/22/code.py:295:    - Only three template ports are controllable: the two endpoints of the active edge and its midpoint. Their rays are anchored at a discrete hub chosen adjacent to the geometric centroid and head in the three cardinal directions that reach those structural ports.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/22/code.py:296:    - If the first non-bg cell beyond a hub ray is an isolated marker, that marker color labels the corresponding template port. Then every transformed sprite emits that color outward from its own matching centroid-side hub ray through bg cells until blocked or out of bounds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/247ef758/D6/1/code.py:68:#     narrower and contain only the framed region\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/36/code.py:27:#         Real sprites have a 2-row / 2-col contact mouth whose protrusion pattern is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/36/code.py:54:#      one-cell protrusion\" can attach there; a bigger same-color blob is ignored.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:33:#       narrow: width == 1, stays blue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:38:#     - recolor only wide frames to teal (8); narrow frames remain blue (1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:50:#   - Every sample contains both narrow and wide frames, so the blue/teal split is observable in 2-3 examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:56:#     That becomes wrong here because all frames have holes but narrow ones must stay blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:145:    - Recolor only wide frames (thickness >= 2) to teal (8); narrow one-pixel frames stay blue (1).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:242:    num_narrow = random.randint(NARROW_COUNT_RANGE[0], min(NARROW_COUNT_RANGE[1], num_components - 1))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:248:    thicknesses = [NARROW_THICKNESS] * num_narrow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:249:    thicknesses.extend(random.choice(wide_choices) for _ in range(num_components - num_narrow))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/1/code.py:46:#   sprite of the wrong contact-length class. Position alone only narrows the search;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D14/0/code.py:23:#     one can only be placed where its centroid stays above the horizontal midline, and the blue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D14/0/code.py:36:#     centroid-band legality check based on the visible upper/lower color families.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/38/code.py:22:#         plus one protrusion band whose 4-bit silhouette matches that side's notch\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/38/code.py:28:#      have a full 4-cell support row just inside the hub and a bottom protrusion row\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/38/code.py:64:#      protrusion mouths.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/58f5dbd5/D2/0/code.py:120:    - Color only narrows the candidate pool; the real stencil is the same-colored motif shape that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/25/code.py:234:    blue-region outlier,\" while the marker has narrowed from an unrestricted\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D4/1/code.py:12:#         and drawn from a narrow zigzag family, so the frame bitmap itself is symmetric across both axes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/3/code.py:28:#     the matching 4-bit protrusion row/col backed by a solid support band.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/3/code.py:44:#     a filled protrusion at that slot. These patterns are pairwise distinct and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/3/code.py:60:#            - the adjacent protrusion lane equals that side's notch pattern\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/3/code.py:75:#     every sample, so humans can infer \"notch <-> protrusion complement\" from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/26/code.py:56:#    which keeps them valid single-step protrusions. Blue spur noise is added\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/35/code.py:31:#           protrusion row = 1000\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/35/code.py:40:#      “底部一整条 support 带 + 最左一格 protrusion”。其它同色组件要么\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/35/code.py:41:#      protrusion 位置不对，要么 support 带不完整，要么多个旋转都不唯一。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/8/code.py:337:    \"\"\"Add isolated 1-cell leaf protrusions that remain true leaves.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/14/code.py:62:#    staircase bites and protrusions, not as a single centered notch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/7/code.py:25:#      但在任何旋转、任何边上都无法形成“support 带全满 + protrusion 带等于该边凹口”\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D10/2/code.py:18:#      enters a progressively narrower corridor and draws nested rectangular\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cb2d8a2c/D10/2/code.py:61:#      path's layer-by-layer penetration into a narrowing channel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/1/code.py:53:#      creates attached 1-pixel protrusions and prevents adjacent leaves that would raise degree.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/12/code.py:53:#      the protrusion extends into.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/19/code.py:56:#      In this combo we also require at least one blue 4-neighbor, so only protrusions into blue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/19/code.py:66:#      black attachment, so they remain one-pixel protrusions instead of thick bridges.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/19/code.py:79:#      means the tip is a protrusion target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/34/code.py:83:   - At the same time, thin black edge protrusions are no longer highlighted, distinguishing the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/15/code.py:369:    \"\"\"Place leaf protrusions from large black regions into adjacent blue territory.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/36/code.py:26:#    black cells. Example on a narrow black stripe:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/36/code.py:479:    \"\"\"Insert a few black leaf protrusions extending from large black regions.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/11/code.py:31:#    - The surviving targets are one-cell black protrusions attached to a large\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/11/code.py:72:#      protrusion after insertion.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/4/code.py:38:#    - Leaves are added as single black protrusions attached to large black regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/58f5dbd5/D16/1/code.py:63:# - The legend uses only a narrow 2-column corner strip with blank rows between pairs, so it is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/38/code.py:46:#      stops placing leaf protrusions so that no unmarked branch tips compete with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/39/code.py:50:#    - Accepted boards always contain both small enclosed defects and at least one leaf protrusion, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/9/code.py:393:    \"\"\"Place separated leaf protrusions from large black regions into blue regions.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/7/code.py:248:    - Neither color alone nor shape frequency alone is sufficient here. Color narrows the search, shape identifies which\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/26/code.py:644:        narrowed = [c for c in subset if score_fn(c) == best]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/26/code.py:645:        if narrowed:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/26/code.py:646:            subset = narrowed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D5/2/code.py:84:    Decide vertical/horizontal flips from a placeholder bbox center relative to the frame center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D5/2/code.py:115:    - For each placeholder block, use its bbox center relative to the frame center to choose reflection axes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/6/code.py:44:#    objects inside a narrow interior activity strip aligned with the long grid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/6/code.py:68:#    Active objects share one narrow strip but do not overlap after expansion.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D16/1/code.py:19:#      New rule: landing = round(centroid(sprite)) + 5*dir.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D16/1/code.py:20:#      For L-shapes the rounded centroid usually stays on the corner pixel, so they often behave as before.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D16/1/code.py:21:#      For V-shapes the rounded centroid is the empty center between the two diagonal legs, one cell behind the apex\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D16/1/code.py:26:#      New: centroid=(8/3,3), rounded start=(3,3), landing=(3,3)+5*(-1,0)=(-2,3). The destination moves down by 1.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D16/1/code.py:29:#    - To keep the D16 change visible, the generator forces at least one V-shape whose centroid-based landing differs\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D16/1/code.py:38:#      centroids only .0/.333/.667 occur, so there is no tie ambiguity in practice.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D16/1/code.py:40:#    - Every placement is precomputed from apex+direction, then converted to centroid-start+direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D16/1/code.py:41:#    - Generator checks: sprite cells in bounds, centroid-based destination in bounds, no 8-neighbor touching,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D16/1/code.py:47:#    - Sprites keep Chebyshev distance >= 2, so the new centroid-start idea does not create merged or unreadable shapes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D16/1/code.py:61:def _rounded_centroid(comp: list[tuple[int, int]] | tuple[tuple[int, int], ...]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D16/1/code.py:120:def _solve(grid: np.ndarray, *, centroid_start: bool) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D16/1/code.py:140:        start = _rounded_centroid(comp) if centroid_start else apex\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D16/1/code.py:175:    - The launch point is no longer the apex pixel. Compute the sprite's 3-pixel centroid, round it to the nearest grid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D16/1/code.py:176:      cell, and place the projectile landing point at rounded-centroid + 5*direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D16/1/code.py:185:    return _solve(grid, centroid_start=True)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D16/1/code.py:188:# --------------- generator (D16 centroid-start variant) ---------------\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D16/1/code.py:245:                start = _rounded_centroid(cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D16/1/code.py:494:    old_out = _solve(inp, centroid_start=False)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/12/code.py:129:    ambiguity in narrow bounding boxes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D3/0/code.py:33:#       every direction is represented by a 3-pixel arrow whose pointed tip is the emitter.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D3/0/code.py:35:#       diagonal directions use 2x2 wedge arrows whose single corner tip points diagonally.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D3/0/code.py:36:#       the solver now matches one of 8 explicit arrow templates instead of classifying\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D3/0/code.py:43:#       cells {(0,0),(1,0),(1,1)} are a NW arrow; the visible lone corner (0,0) is the tip,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D3/0/code.py:49:#     - Force each generated grid to contain at least two diagonal arrows and at least one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D3/0/code.py:50:#       axis arrow; otherwise the input could look too similar to the original task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D3/0/code.py:56:#       the old L/V formulas. This must be replaced by explicit arrow templates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D3/0/code.py:65:#     - The diagonal sprites now look like literal diagonal arrowheads instead of old \"L with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D3/0/code.py:66:#       a missing-corner rule\". Because each grid is required to include diagonal arrows, the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D3/0/code.py:69:#     - Output markers stay single-cell and sprites remain sparse, so arrows and landing marks\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D3/0/code.py:111:def _arrow_tip_and_dir(comp: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int]] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D3/0/code.py:112:    \"\"\"Return (tip_rc, dir_rc) for a 3-pixel arrow sprite, else No